ue - Cost of baking = \\$93 - \\$15 = \\$78\n\n### Step 3: Find the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence\n\nThe sequence starts with 2, and each subsequent term increases by consecutive odd numbers. So the sequence is:\n\\[2, 2+3, 2+3+5, 2+3+5+7, \\ldots\\]\n\nThe \\(n\\)-th term of the sequence can be written as:\n\\[a_n = 2 + \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} (2i+1)\\]\n\\[a_n = 2 + (1 + 3 + 5 + \\cdots + (2n-3))\\]\nThe sum of the first \\(n-1\\) odd numbers is \\((n-1)^2\\), so:\n\\[a_n = 2 + (n-1)^2\\]\n\nThe first 10 terms of the sequence are:\n\\[2, 5, 10, 17, 26, 37, 50, 65, 82, 101\\]\n\nThe sum of the first 10 terms is:\n\\[2 + 5 + 10 + 17 + 26 + 37 + 50 + 65 + 82 + 101\\]\n\nWe can calculate this sum using Python to ensure accuracy.\n\nLet's implement this in Python.\n```python\n# Calculate the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence\nterms = [2 + (n-1)**2 for n in range(1, 11)]\nsum_of_terms = sum(terms)\nprint((sum_of_terms, 78))\n```\n```output\n(395, 78)\n```\nThe sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence is \\(395\\), and the profit from the bake sale is \\(\\$78\\).\n\nSo the final answers are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{78} \\quad \\text{(profit)}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\boxed{395} \\quad \\text{(sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence)}\n\\]", 'A triangle has side lengths of $13$, $14$, and $15$. What is the smallest angle in this triangle? \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. 