 perimeter of the hexagon is \\(6 \\times 16 = 96\\) cm. Since the regular octagon has the same perimeter as the hexagon, the perimeter of the octagon is also 96 cm. A regular octagon has 8 sides, so each side of the octagon is \\( \\frac{96}{8} = 12 \\) cm long.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Number of sides of the hexagon\nnum_sides_hexagon = 6\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = side_length_hexagon * num_sides_hexagon\n\n# Number of sides of the octagon\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe side length of each side of the octagon is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm.", "To determine the side length of the regular octagon, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the perimeter of the regular hexagon.\n2. Use the perimeter of the hexagon to determine the perimeter of the octagon.\n3. Divide the perimeter of the octagon by 8 to find the side length of the octagon.\n\nLet's start by calculating the perimeter of the regular hexagon. Since a hexagon has 6 sides and each side is 16 cm, the perimeter of the hexagon is \\(6 \\times 16 = 96\\) cm.\n\nSince the regular octagon has the same perimeter as the hexagon, the perimeter of the octagon is also 96 cm. An octagon has 8 sides, so the side length of the octagon is \\( \\frac{96}{8} = 12 \\) cm.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Number of sides of the hexagon\nnum_sides_hexagon = 6\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = side_length_hexagon * num_sides_hexagon\n\n# Number of sides of the octagon\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe side length of the regular octagon is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm.", "To find the length of each side of the regular octagon, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the perimeter of the regular hexagon.\n2. Since the perimeters of the hexagon and the octagon are equal, use the perimeter of the hexagon to find the side length of the octagon.\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n1. **Calculate the Perimeter of the Hexagon:**\n   - A regular hexagon has 6 equal sides.\n   - Each side of the hexagon is 16 cm.\n   - Therefore, the perimeter \\(P_{\\text{hexagon}}\\) of the hexagon is:\n     \\[\n     P_{\\text{hexagon}} = 6 \\times 16 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the Side Length of the Octagon:**\n   - A regular octagon has 8 equal sides.\n   - Let \\(s_{\\text{octagon}}\\) be the side length of the octagon.\n   - The perimeter \\(P_{\\text{octagon}}\\) of the octagon is:\n     \\[\n     P_{\\text{octagon}} = 8 \\times s_{\\text{octagon}}\n     \\]\n   - Since the perimeters of the hexagon and the octagon are equal:\n     \\[\n     6 \\times 16 = 8 \\times s_{\\text{octagon}}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\(s_{\\text{octagon}}\\):**\n   \\[\n   s_{\\text{octagon}} = \\frac{6 \\times 16}{8}\n   \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given data\nside_length_hexagon = 16  # in cm\nnum_sides_hexagon = 6\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = num_sides_hexagon * side_length_hexagon\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe length of each side of the regular octagon is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the side length of a regular octagon that has the same perimeter as a regular hexagon with a side length of 16 cm.\n\n1. **Calculate the Perimeter of the Hexagon:**\n   A regular hexagon has 6 sides. If each side is 16 cm, then the perimeter \\(P_{\\text{hexagon}}\\) of the hexagon is:\n   \\[\n   P_{\\text{hexagon}} = 6 \\times 16 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the Perimeter of the Octagon:**\n   The perimeter of the octagon \\(P_{\\text{octagon}}\\) is the same as the perimeter of the hexagon. An octagon has 8 sides. Let \\(s\\) be the side length of the octagon. Then:\n   \\[\n   P_{\\text{octagon}} = 8 \\times s\n   \\]\n\n3. **Set the Perimeters Equal and Solve for \\(s\\):**\n   Since the perimeters are equal:\n   \\[\n   8 \\times s = 6 \\times 16\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\(s\\):\n   \\[\n   s = \\frac{6 \\times 16}{8}\n   \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Number of sides in the hexagon and octagon\nnum_sides_hexagon = 6\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = num_sides_hexagon * side_length_hexagon\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe side length of the octagon is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm.", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the side length of a regular octagon that has the same perimeter as a regular hexagon with a side length of 16 cm.\n\n1. First, we calculate the perimeter of the hexagon.\n2. Since the perimeter of the hexagon is equal to the perimeter of the octagon, we use this value to find the side length of the octagon.\n\nA regular hexagon has 6 sides, so its perimeter is \\(6 \\times 16 = 96\\) cm.\n\nA regular octagon has 8 sides, and since its perimeter is equal to the perimeter of the hexagon, we can set up the equation:\n\\[8 \\times \\text{side length of the octagon} = 96\\]\n\nSolving for the side length of the octagon:\n\\[\\text{side length of the octagon} = \\frac{96}{8} = 12 \\text{ cm}\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given 