rac{3}{4}\\right)^2}$.\n\nLet's implement this in Python to find the direct distance.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the distances\ndistance_south = 1\ndistance_east = sp.Rational(3, 4)\n\n# Calculate the direct distance using the Pythagorean theorem\ndirect_distance = sp.sqrt(distance_south**2 + distance_east**2)\n\n# Evaluate the direct distance to the nearest hundredth\ndirect_distance_decimal = round(direct_distance.evalf(), 2)\n\nprint(direct_distance_decimal)\n```\n```output\n1.25\n```\nThe direct distance from Bill's starting point after walking $\\frac{1}{2}$ mile south, then $\\frac{3}{4}$ mile east, and finally another $\\frac{1}{2}$ mile south is \\(\\boxed{1.25}\\) miles.", 'Given the equation $y = 2x^2 + 3x - 5$, what is the value of $y$ when $x = 3$?  Express your answer as a decimal to the nearest tenth.  \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}.