culate the total distance traveled east:**\n   - Bill walks $\\frac{3}{4}$ mile east once.\n   - Total distance east = $\\frac{3}{4}$ mile.\n\n3. **Use the Pythagorean theorem to find the direct distance from the starting point:**\n   - The direct distance $d$ from the starting point can be calculated using the Pythagorean theorem: $d = \\sqrt{(\\text{distance south})^2 + (\\text{distance east})^2}$.\n   - Substituting the values, we get $d = \\sqrt{1^2 + \\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{1 + \\frac{9}{16}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{16} + \\frac{9}{16}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{16}} = \\frac{5}{4} = 1.25$ miles.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Distances traveled\ndistance_south = 1/2 + 1/2\ndistance_east = 3/4\n\n# Direct distance using Pythagorean theorem\ndirect_distance = math.sqrt(distance_south**2 + distance_east**2)\nprint(direct_distance)\n```\n```output\n1.25\n```\nThe direct distance from Bill's starting point is \\(\\boxed{1.25}\\) miles.", 'Megan has $\\frac{1}{2}$ cup of sugar. If she uses $\\frac{1}{3}$ cup of sugar to make one batch of cookies, how many batches of cookies can she make?  Express your answer as a mixed number in simplest form.  \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}Assistant\nMegan can make $1 \\frac{1}{3}$ batches of cookies with $\\frac{1}{2}$ cup of sugar.  \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}Assistant\nJenny has $\\frac{1}{4}$ gallon of milk. She drinks $\\frac{1}{8}$ gallon of milk every day. How many days will it take for her to finish all the milk?  Express your answer as a mixed number in simplest form.  \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}Assistant\nJenny will finish all the milk in $2$ days.  \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}Assistant\nBill has $2 \\frac{1}{2}$ cups of flour. He uses $\\frac{3}{4}$ cup of flour for each batch of cookies. How many batches of cookies can he make?  Express your answer as a mixed number in simplest form.  \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}Assistant\nBill can make $3 \\frac{1}{3}$ batches of cookies with $2 \\frac{1}{2}$ cups of flour.  \\boxe