al to 8 is \\( \\frac{3}{2} \\).\n\n### Part 2: Calculate the sum of the interior angles of a convex polygon with 11 sides\n\nThe sum of the interior angles of a convex polygon with \\( n \\) sides is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Sum of interior angles} = (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ \\]\n\nFor a polygon with 11 sides:\n\n\\[ \\text{Sum of interior angles} = (11-2) \\times 180^\\circ = 9 \\times 180^\\circ = 1620^\\circ \\]\n\nIn radians, the sum of the interior angles is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Sum of interior angles in radians} = (n-2) \\times \\pi \\]\n\\[ \\text{Sum of interior angles in radians} = (11-2) \\times \\pi = 9\\pi \\]\n\nSo, the sum of the interior angles of a convex polygon with 11 sides is \\( 1620^\\circ \\) or \\( 9\\pi \\) radians.\n\nLet's summarize the results:\n\n1. The power of 4 that is equal to 8 is \\( \\frac{3}{2} \\).\n2. The sum of the interior angles of a convex polygon with 11 sides is \\( 1620^\\circ \\) or \\( 9\\pi \\) radians.\n\nThe final answers are:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}} \\]\n\\[ \\boxed{1620} \\]\n\\[ \\boxed{9\\pi} \\]\n\nHere is the Python code to verify these calculations:\n\n```python\n# Part 1: Calculate the power of 4 that is equal to 8\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the variable\nx = symbols('x')\n\n# Define the equation 4^x = 8\nequation = Eq(4**x, 8)\n\n# Solve the equation\nsolution = solve(equation, x)\npower_of_4 = solution[0]\n\n# Part 2: Calculate the sum of the interior angles of a convex polygon with 11 sides\nn = 11\nsum_of_interior_angles_degrees = (n - 2) * 180\nsum_of_interior_angles_radians = (n - 2) * 3.141592653589793\n\nprint(power_of_4, sum_of_interior_angles_degrees, sum_of_interior_angles_radians)\n```", "To determine what power of 4 is equal to 8, we need to find \\( x \\) in the equation \\( 4^x = 8 \\). We can solve this by expressing both 4 and 8 as powers of 2, since \\( 4 = 2^2 \\) and \\( 8 = 2^3 \\). This transforms the equation to \\( (2^2)^x = 2^3 \\), which simplifies 