n   \\frac{1}{2}(3x - 9) = x + 37\n   \\]\n\n2. Eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides by 2:\n   \\[\n   3x - 9 = 2(x + 37)\n   \\]\n\n3. Distribute the 2 on the right side:\n   \\[\n   3x - 9 = 2x + 74\n   \\]\n\n4. Isolate \\(x\\) by subtracting \\(2x\\) from both sides:\n   \\[\n   x - 9 = 74\n   \\]\n\n5. Add 9 to both sides to solve for \\(x\\):\n   \\[\n   x = 83\n   \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{83}\\).\n\n### Problem 2: The area of a square is 196 square units. What is the length of one side of the square, in units?\n\n1. Recall that the area \\(A\\) of a square is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   A = s^2\n   \\]\n   where \\(s\\) is the length of one side of the square.\n\n2. Substitute the given area into the formula:\n   \\[\n   196 = s^2\n   \\]\n\n3. Solve for \\(s\\) by taking the square root of both sides:\n   \\[\n   s = \\sqrt{196}\n   \\]\n\n4. Calculate the square root:\n   \\[\n   s = 14\n   \\]\n\nSo, the length of one side of the square is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).\n\n### Problem 3: What is the value of \\(x\\) if \\(x\\) is the number of sides of a polygon that has a total interior angle sum of 1080 degrees?\n\n1. Recall that the sum of the interior angles of a polygon with \\(n\\) sides is given by the formula:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Sum of interior angles} = (n-2) \\times 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n2. Substitute the given sum of interior angles into the formula:\n   \\[\n   1080 = (n-2) \\times 180\n   \\]\n\n3. Solve for \\(n\\) by dividing both sides by 180:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1080}{180} = n - 2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   6 = n - 2\n   \\]\n\n4. Add 2 to both sides to solve for \\(n\\):\n   \\[\n   n = 8\n   \\]\n\nSo, the number of sides of the polygon is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).\n\n### Problem 4: If \\(x\\) is the number of days in a non-leap year, what is the value of \\(x\\)?\n\n1. Recall that a non-leap year has 365 days.\n\n2. Therefore, the value of \\(x\\) is:\n   \\[\n   x = 365\n   \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{365}\