a, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). This will help us to simplify the numerator of each fraction.\n\nLet's break it down step by step for each expression:\n\n1. For the expression \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{2.5^2 - 0.7^2}}{2.7 - 2.5}\\):\n   - The numerator \\(\\sqrt{2.5^2 - 0.7^2}\\) can be simplified using the difference of squares formula:\n     \\[\n     2.5^2 - 0.7^2 = (2.5 - 0.7)(2.5 + 0.7) = 1.8 \\cdot 3.2\n     \\]\n   - So, the expression becomes:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{\\sqrt{1.8 \\cdot 3.2}}{2.7 - 2.5} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5.76}}{0.2} = \\frac{2.4}{0.2} = 12\n     \\]\n\n2. For the expression \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{4.9^2 - 2.8^2}}{3.6 - 3.2}\\):\n   - The numerator \\(\\sqrt{4.9^2 - 2.8^2}\\) can be simplified using the difference of squares formula:\n     \\[\n     4.9^2 - 2.8^2 = (4.9 - 2.8)(4.9 + 2.8) = 2.1 \\cdot 7.7\n     \\]\n   - So, the expression becomes:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{\\sqrt{2.1 \\cdot 7.7}}{3.6 - 3.2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{16.17}}{0.4} = \\frac{4.021201967434218}{0.4} \\approx 10.053\n     \\]\n\nLet's implement this in Python to get the exact values:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the expressions\nexpr1 = sp.sqrt(2.5**2 - 0.7**2) / (2.7 - 2.5)\nexpr2 = sp.sqrt(4.9**2 - 2.8**2) / (3.6 - 3.2)\n\n# Simplify the expressions\nsimplified_expr1 = sp.simplify(expr1)\nsimplified_expr2 = sp.simplify(expr2)\n\nprint(simplified_expr1)\nprint(simplified_expr2)\n```\n```output\n12.0000000000000\n10.0530700515397\n```\nThe simplified values of the given expressions are:\n\n1. \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{2.5^2 - 0.7^2}}{2.7 - 2.5} = 12\\)\n2. \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{4.9^2 - 2.8^2}}{3.6 - 3.2} \\approx 10.053\\)\n\nSo, the final answers are:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\boxed{10.053}\n\\]", 'Simplify: $\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{108}}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{48}}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{75}}$. Shaymin2\nSimplify: $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{18}}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{32}}+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{50}}$. Eugenius1512\nSimplify: $\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{18}}+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{32}}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{50}}$. AopsUser10