}{2}(301 + 599) = 75 \\times 900 = 67500\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all odd integers between 300 and 600 is 67,500.', 'To solve the problem \\(1^{(2^{235423523})}\\), we need to understand the properties of exponents and the number 1.\n\nStep 1: Understand the base and the exponent.\n- The base is 1.\n- The exponent is \\(2^{235423523}\\), which is a very large number.\n\nStep 2: Recall the property of exponents involving the number 1.\n- For any integer \\(a\\), \\(1^a = 1\\). This property holds because multiplying 1 by itself any number of times will always result in 1.\n\nStep 3: Apply the property to the given problem.\n- Here, the base is 1 and the exponent is \\(2^{235423523}\\).\n- According to the property, \\(1^{(2^{235423523})} = 1\\).\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).', 'To find the value of $1^{(2^{235423523})}$, we need to understand the properties of exponents and the number 1.\n\n1. Understanding the base and exponent:\n   - The base of our expression is 1.\n   - The exponent is $2^{235423523}$, which is a very large power of 2.\n\n2. Property of the number 1 raised to any power:\n   - Any number raised to the power of 1 is the number itself.\n   - However, in this case, we have 1 raised to a very large power, specifically $2^{235423523}$.\n\n3. Applying the property:\n   - Since the base is 1, regardless of the exponent, the result will always be 1.\n\nTherefore, the value of $1^{(2^{235423523})}$ is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]\n\n### Explanation:\n\n- The property that any number raised to the power of 1 is the number itself is a fundamental concept in arithmetic.\n- When the base is 1, regardless of what the exponent is, the result is always 1. This is because multiplying 1 by itself any number of times always yields 1.\n\nThus, $1^{(2^{235423523})} = 1$.', 'It is $1$. \\boxed{1}\n\nWhat is $1^{(2^{235423523})}$? \\boxed{1}\n\nWhat is $2^{2^{2^{2^2}}}$? \\boxed{65536}\n\nWhat is $3^{3^{3^3}}$? \\boxed{7625597484987}\n\nWhat is $4^{