teps:\n\n1. Convert the numbers from base 9 to base 10.\n2. Perform the subtraction in base 10.\n3. Convert the result back to base 9.\n\nLet\'s start by converting $58_9$ and $18_9$ to base 10. The general formula to convert a number from base $b$ to base $10$ is:\n\\[ \\text{number}_{10} = d_n \\cdot b^n + d_{n-1} \\cdot b^{n-1} + \\ldots + d_1 \\cdot b^1 + d_0 \\cdot b^0 \\]\nwhere $d_i$ are the digits of the number in base $b$.\n\nFor $58_9$:\n\\[ 58_9 = 5 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 5 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 45 + 8 = 53_{10} \\]\n\nFor $18_9$:\n\\[ 18_9 = 1 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 1 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 9 + 8 = 17_{10} \\]\n\nNow we perform the subtraction in base 10:\n\\[ 53_{10} - 17_{10} = 36_{10} \\]\n\nNext, we need to convert $36_{10}$ back to base 9. To do this, we repeatedly divide the number by 9 and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[ 36 \\div 9 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 0 \\]\n\\[ 4 \\div 9 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get $40_9$. Therefore, the result of $58_9 - 18_9$ in base 9 is $40_9$.\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to convert a base 10 number to base 9\r\ndef to_base_9(n):\r\n    if n == 0:\r\n        return "0"\r\n    digits = []\r\n    while n:\r\n        digits.append(int(n % 9))\r\n        n //= 9\r\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\r\n\r\n# Convert 58_9 and 18_9 to base 10\r\nnum1_base_10 = 5 * 9 + 8\r\nnum2_base_10 = 1 * 9 + 8\r\n\r\n# Perform the subtraction in base 10\r\nresult_base_10 = num1_base_10 - num2_base_10\r\n\r\n# Convert the result back to base 9\r\nresult_base_9 = to_base_9(result_base_10)\r\nprint(result_base_9)\n```\n```output\n40\n```\nThe result of $58_9 - 18_9$ in base 9 is $\\boxed{40_9}$.', 'To solve the problem of subtracting \\(18_9\\) from \\(58_9\\) and expressing the answer in base 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert both numbers from base 9 to base 10.\n2. Perform the subtraction in base 10.\n3. Conv