thon\nimport math\n\n# Total number of letters\nn = 11\n# Frequencies of each letter\nfreq = [2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]\n\n# Calculate the number of unique anagrams\nunique_anagrams = math.factorial(n)\nfor f in freq:\n    unique_anagrams //= math.factorial(f)\n\nprint(unique_anagrams)\n```\n```output\n4989600\n```\nThe number of unique anagrams of the word "MATHEMATICS" is \\(\\boxed{4989600}\\).\n\n### Problem 2: Probability of Product Being a Multiple of 5\nWe need to find the probability that the product of the numbers on two fair 6-sided dice is a multiple of 5. The numbers on a 6-sided die are \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6\\}. The product will be a multiple of 5 if at least one of the dice shows a 5.\n\nLet\'s calculate the probability step by step:\n1. The probability that the first die shows a 5 is \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\).\n2. The probability that the second die shows a 5 is \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\).\n3. The probability that both dice show a 5 is \\(\\frac{1}{6} \\times \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{36}\\).\n4. The probability that the product is a multiple of 5 is the probability that at least one die shows a 5, which is \\(1 - \\text{probability that neither die shows a 5}\\).\n5. The probability that neither die shows a 5 is \\(\\frac{5}{6} \\times \\frac{5}{6} = \\frac{25}{36}\\).\n6. Therefore, the probability that the product is a multiple of 5 is \\(1 - \\frac{25}{36} = \\frac{11}{36}\\).\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python.\n```python\n# Total number of outcomes when two dice are rolled\ntotal_outcomes = 6 * 6\n\n# Number of outcomes where the product is a multiple of 5\nmultiple_of_5_outcomes = 0\n\n# Iterate through all possible outcomes\nfor i in range(1, 7):\n    for j in range(1, 7):\n        if (i * j) % 5 == 0:\n            multiple_of_5_outcomes += 1\n\n# Probability that the product is a multiple of 5\nprobability_multiple_of_5 = multiple_of_5_outcomes / total_outcomes\nprint(probability_multiple_of_5)\n```', 'A game is played where a player picks two marbles from a bag