\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify the numerator and the denominator separately using trigonometric identities.\n\n### Simplifying the Numerator\n\nThe numerator is:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ\n\\]\n\nWe can use the identity $\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos(A + B)$ to simplify the first and third terms, and the identity $\\cos A \\cos B + \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos(A - B)$ to simplify the second and fourth terms. Thus, the numerator becomes:\n\\[\n\\cos(5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) + \\cos(35^\\circ - 50^\\circ) = \\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos(-15^\\circ) = \\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 15^\\circ\n\\]\n\n### Simplifying the Denominator\n\nThe denominator is:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ\n\\]\n\nWe can use the identity $\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin(A + B)$ to simplify the first and third terms, and the identity $\\sin A \\cos B - \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin(A - B)$ to simplify the second and fourth terms. Thus, the denominator becomes:\n\\[\n\\sin(5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) - \\sin(35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ = \\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ\n\\]\n\n### Final Expression\n\nSo, the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 15^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nWe can use Python to evaluate this expression and find the least positive angle $\\theta$.\n\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Define the angles in degrees\nangle_25 = math.radians(25)\nangle_15 = math.radians(15)\nangle_5 = math.radians(5)\n\n# Calculate the numerator and denominator\nnumerator = math.cos(angle_25) + math.cos(angle_15)\ndenominator = math.sin(angle_25) - math.cos(angle_5)\n\n#