nominator separately.\n\n### Simplifying the Numerator\nThe numerator is:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\nWe can group the terms as follows:\n\\[\n(\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ) + (\\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ).\n\\]\nUsing the cosine addition formula, $\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos(A + B)$, we get:\n\\[\n\\cos(5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) + \\cos(35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ.\n\\]\n\n### Simplifying the Denominator\nThe denominator is:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\nWe can group the terms as follows:\n\\[\n(\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ) - (\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ).\n\\]\nUsing the sine addition formula, $\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin(A + B)$, we get:\n\\[\n\\sin(5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) - \\sin(35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ.\n\\]\n\n### Simplifying the Expression\nNow we can rewrite the original expression as:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ}.\n\\]\nUsing the sum-to-product identities, we have:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos (-30^\\circ) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\sqrt{3} \\cos 55^\\circ.\n\\]\nAnd,\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin (-30^\\circ) = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = -\\cos 55^\\circ.\n\\]\nSo, the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} \\cos 55^\\circ}{-\\cos 55^\\circ} = -\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\nThe angle $\\theta$ for which $\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}$ is $\\theta = 120^\\circ$ or $\\theta = 3', "To solve the given problem, we need to simplify the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ and find the corresponding angle $\\theta$. Let's start by simplifying the numerator and the denominator separately.\n\nThe given expression is:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}{\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the trigonometric identities:\n\\[\n\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos (A + B),\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin (A + B).\n\\]\n\nLet's simplify the numerator and the denominator using these identities.\n\n### Simplifying the Numerator\nThe numerator is:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\nWe can group the terms as follows:\n\\[\n(\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ) + (\\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ).\n\\]\nUsing the identity $\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos (A + B)$, we get:\n\\[\n\\cos (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) + \\cos (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ.\n\\]\nUsing the identity $\\cos (90^\\circ - x) = \\sin x$, we get:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ.\n\\]\n\n### Simplifying the Denominator\nThe denominator is:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\nWe can group the terms as follows:\n\\[\n(\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ) - (\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ).\n\\]\nUsing the identity $\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin (A + B)$, we get:\n\\[\n\\sin (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) - \\sin (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ.\n\\]\nUsing the identity $\\sin (90^\\circ - x) = \\cos x$, we get:\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ.\n\\]\n\n### Simplifying the Expression\nNow we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ}.\n\\]\nWe can use the identity $\\sin (90^\\circ - x) = \\cos x$ and $\\cos (90^\\circ - x) = \\sin x$ to further simplify:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ} = \\frac{\\sin 65^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ}{\\cos 65^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ}.\n\\]\nUsing the sum-to-product identities:\n\\[\n\\sin A + \\sin B = 2 \\sin \\left(\\frac{A + B}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{A - B}{2}\\right),\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos A - \\cos B = -2 \\sin \\left(\\frac{A + B}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{A - B}{2}\\right),\n\\]\n", "To solve the given problem, we need to simplify the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ and then find the corresponding angle $\\theta$. Let's break down the problem step by step.\n\nThe given expression for $\\tan \\theta$ is:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}{\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use trigonometric identities to simplify the numerator and the denominator. Notice that the numerator can be rewritten using the cosine addition formula:\n\\[\n\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos (A + B).\n\\]\n\nSo, we can rewrite the numerator as:\n\\[\n\\cos (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) + \\cos (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\