rac{1}{2} [\\sin 85^\\circ - \\sin 15^\\circ],\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin (-15", "To solve the given problem, we need to simplify the expression for $\\tan \\theta$. Let's start by examining the numerator and the denominator separately.\n\nThe numerator is:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\nWe can use the identity $\\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B = \\cos (A + B)$ to simplify the terms involving cosine and sine products. Thus, we can rewrite the numerator as:\n\\[\n\\cos (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) + \\cos (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ.\n\\]\nUsing the identity $\\cos (90^\\circ - x) = \\sin x$, we get $\\cos 85^\\circ = \\sin 5^\\circ$. So the numerator simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThe denominator is:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ.\n\\]\nWe can use the identity $\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin (A + B)$ to simplify the terms involving sine and cosine products. Thus, we can rewrite the denominator as:\n\\[\n\\sin (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) - \\sin (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = \\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ.\n\\]\nUsing the identity $\\sin (90^\\circ - x) = \\cos x$, we get $\\sin 85^\\circ = \\cos 5^\\circ$. So the denominator simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\sin 5^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\cos 5^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nTo find the angle $\\theta$, we need to determine the angle whose tangent is equal to the simplified expression. Let's use Python to calculate the value of $\\theta$.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the value of the simplified expression\nnumerator = math.cos(math.radians(25)) +