 until we find a repeating cycle.\n\n1. Calculate $z_1 = F(z_0)$:\n\\[ z_1 = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) + i}{\\left(\\frac{1}{137} + i\\right) - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i \\]\n\n2. Calculate $z_2 = F(z_1)$:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{(1 + 274i) + i}{(1 + 274i) - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i} \\]\nTo simplify, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i + 74775}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74776 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37388}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i \\]\n\n3. Calculate $z_3 = F(z_2)$:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{37388}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\right) + i}{\\left(\\frac{37388}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\right) - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37388}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i}{\\frac{37388}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i} = \\frac{37388 + 37266i}{37388 - 37264i} \\]\nAgain, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{(37388 + 37266i)(37388 + 37264i)}{(37388 - 37264i)(37388 + 37264i)} = \\frac{1397774544 + 1397774528i + 1397774528i - 1397774544}{1397774544 + 1397774544} = \\frac{2795549056i}{2795549088} = i \\]\n\n4. Calculate $z_4 = F(z_3)$:\n\\[ z_4 = F(i) = \\frac{i + i}{i - i} = \\frac{2i}{0} \\]\nThis is undefined, so we need to handle this case separately. Since $z_3 = i$, we can see that $z_4 = F(i) = \\infty$, and for all subsequent terms, $z_n = \\infty$.\n\nHowever, we can see that the sequence repeats every 3 terms after the first term. So, we can use the modulo operation to", "To solve the problem, we need to understand the behavior of the function \\( F(z) = \\frac{z + i}{z - i} \\) and how it transforms the sequence \\( z_n \\). We will compute the first few terms of the sequence to identify any patterns.\n\nGiven:\n\\[ z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i \\]\n\\[ z_{n} = F(z_{n-1}) = \\frac{z_{n-1} + i}{z_{n-1} - i} \\]\n\nLet's compute the first few terms of the sequence to see if we can identify a pattern.\n\n1. Compute \\( z_1 \\):\n\\[ z_1 = F(z_0) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + i + i}{\\frac{1}{137} + i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i \\]\n\n2. Compute \\( z_2 \\):\n\\[ z_2 = F(z_1) = \\frac{1 + 274i + i}{1 + 274i - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i} \\]\nTo simplify this, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i + 74525}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74526 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i \\]\n\n3. Compute \\( z_3 \\):\n\\[ z_3 = F(z_2) = F\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\right) = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i + i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i} \\]\nAgain, we simplify by multiplying the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i\\right)\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37264}{37265}i\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i\\right)\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37264}{37265}i\\right)} = \\frac{\\frac{37263^2}{37265^2} + \\frac{37263 \\cdot 37264}{37265^2}i + \\frac{37263 \\cdot 37264}{37265^2}i - \\frac{37266 \\cdot 37264}{37265^2}}{\\frac{37263^2}{37265^2} + \\frac{37264^2}{37265^2}} = \\frac{\\frac{37263^2 - 37266 \\cdot 37264}{37265^2} + \\frac{2 \\cdot 37263 \\cdot 37264}{37265^2}i}{\\frac{37263^2 + 37264^2}{3", "To solve this problem, we need to understand the behavior of the function \\(F(z) = \\frac{z + i}{z - i}\\) and how it transforms the sequence \\(z_n = F(z_{n-1})\\). We can start by calculating the first few terms of the sequence to see if there is a pattern.\n\nGiven:\n\\[ z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i \\]\n\nWe need to find \\(z_1 = F(z_0)\\), \\(z_2 = F(z_1)\\), and so on, until we can identify a pattern or cycle.\n\nLet's calculate \\(z_1\\):\n\\[ z_1 = F(z_0) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + i + i}{\\frac{1}{137} + i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate \\(z_2\\):\n\\[ z_2 = F(z_1) = \\frac{1 + 274i + i}{1 + 274i - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i} \\]\nTo simplify this, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i + 74525}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74526 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i \\]\n\nLet's calculate \\(z_3\\):\n\\[ z_3 = F(z_2) = F\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i\\right) = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i + i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i} = \\frac{37263 + 37266i}{37263 - 37264i} \\]\nAgain, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{(37263 + 37266i)(37263 + 37264i)}{(37263 - 37264i)(37263 + 37264i)} = \\frac{1388789369 + 1388789352i + 1388789352i - 1388789344}{1388789369 + 1388789344} = \\frac{5 + 274i}{5} = 1 + \\frac{274}{5}i = 1 + 54.8i \\]\n\nWe can see that the sequence is not immediately simplifying into a recognizable pattern. However, we can use Python to compute the sequence and check for periodicity.\n\nLet's write a Python function to compute the sequence and check for periodicity.\n```python\nimport cmath\n\n# Define the function F(z)\ndef F(z):\n    return (z + 1j) / (z - 1j)\n\n# Initial value\nz = complex(1/137, 1)\n\n# Compute the first few terms of the sequence to check for periodicity\nsequence = [z]\nfor _ in range(20):\n    z = F(z)\n    sequence.append(z)\n\nprint(sequence)\n```\n```output\n[(0.0072992700729927005+1j), (1+", "To solve the problem, we need to understand the behavior of the function \\( F(z) =