-----------|\n| 15  | Monday          |\n| 16  | Tuesday         |\n| 17  | Wednesday       |\n| 18  | Thursday        |\n| 19  | Friday          |\n| 20  | Saturday        |\n| 21  | Sunday          |\n| 22  | Monday          |\n| 23  | Tuesday         |\n| 24  | Wednesday       |\n| 25  | Thursday        |\n| 26  | Friday          |\n| 27  | Saturday        |\n| 28  | Sunday          |\n\n3. To find the fewest number of miles Suzanne can walk in February, we need to determine which days of the month are the third day of a week (i.e., the 3rd, 10th, 17th, and 24th). On these days, Suzanne walks four miles. The other days, she does not walk. Therefore, the fewest number of miles she can walk in February is:\n\n\\[ 4 \\text{ miles/day} \\times 4 \\text{ days} = 16 \\text{ miles} \\]\n\n4. To find the fewest number of miles Suzanne can walk in February, we need to determine which days of the month are the third day of a week (i.e., the 3rd, 10th, 17th, and 24th). On these days, Suzanne walks four miles. The other days, she does not walk. Therefore, the fewest number of miles she can walk in February is:\n\n\\[ 4 \\text{ miles/day} \\times 4 \\text{ days} = 16 \\text{ miles} \\]\n\nThe final answers are:\n\n1. The days of the week for the first 14 days are: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday.\n2. The days of the week for the last 14 days are: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday.\n3. The fewest number of miles Suzanne can walk in February is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).\n4. The fewest number of miles Suzanne can walk in February is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).', 'Alicia has 150 stickers. She wants to give them out to her 20 best friends. If she wants to give out the same amount to each friend, how many stickers will she have left over? \\boxed{Suzanne walks four miles every third day. What is the fewest number