 sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral is \\( 360^\\circ \\), we can set up the following equation:\n\n\\[ x + 2x + 90 + 90 = 360 \\]\n\nSimplifying this equation:\n\n\\[ 3x + 180 = 360 \\]\n\nNow, we solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ 3x = 360 - 180 \\]\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\\[ x = 60 \\]\n\nSo, the smallest angle \\( x \\) is \\( 60^\\circ \\). The largest angle, which is twice the smallest angle, is:\n\n\\[ 2x = 2 \\times 60 = 120^\\circ \\]\n\nLet's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\n# Define the smallest angle\nx = 60\n\n# Calculate the largest angle\nlargest_angle = 2 * x\n\n# Print the result\nprint(largest_angle)\n```\n```output\n120\n```\nThe measure of the largest angle in the convex quadrilateral is \\(\\boxed{120}\\) degrees.", "To solve the problem, we need to use the properties of the angles in a convex quadrilateral. The sum of the interior angles of a quadrilateral is always 360 degrees. Let's denote the smallest angle by \\(x\\). According to the problem, the largest angle is twice the smallest angle, so it is \\(2x\\). The other two angles are both right angles, so they are each 90 degrees.\n\nThe sum of these angles is:\n\\[x + 2x + 90 + 90 = 360\\]\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\\[3x + 180 = 360\\]\nSubtract 180 from both sides:\n\\[3x = 180\\]\nDivide by 3:\n\\[x = 60\\]\nSo the smallest angle is 60 degrees. The largest angle is twice the smallest angle, so it is \\(2 \\times 60 = 120\\) degrees.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the smallest angle as x\nx = 60\n\n# Calculate the largest angle\nlargest_angle = 2 * x\n\n# Print the largest angle\nprint(largest_angle)\n```\n```output\n120\n```\nThe measure of the largest angle in the convex quadrilateral is \\(\\boxed{120}\\) degrees.", 'In a convex quadrilateral, the measure of the largest angle is twice the measure of the smallest angle, and the other two angles are both right angles. How many degrees are in the largest angle? \\boxed{120}\n\\boxed{120}\nIn a