.array([1, 2, 3])\nOB = np.array([-3, -2, 1])\n\n# Calculate the cross product of OA and OB\ncross_product = np.cross(OA, OB)\n\n# Calculate the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\n\n# Calculate the area of the triangle\narea = 0.5 * magnitude\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n6.708203932499369\n```\nThe calculated area of the triangle \\(OAB\\) is \\(3\\sqrt{5}\\), which is approximately 6.708. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]", "The points $O,$ $A,$ and $B$ satisfy $\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$  Find the area of triangle $OAB.$\n\nTo find the area of triangle \\(OAB\\), we can use the fact that the area of a triangle formed by vectors \\(\\overrightarrow{OA}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{OB}\\) is half the magnitude of the cross product of these vectors. The cross product of two vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} u_1 \\\\ u_2 \\\\ u_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\\\ v_2 \\\\ v_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} u_2 v_3 - u_3 v_2 \\\\ u_3 v_1 - u_1 v_3 \\\\ u_1 v_2 - u_2 v_1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nThe magnitude of the cross product vector is then:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\| = \\sqrt{(u_2 v_3 - u_3 v_2)^2 + (u_3 v_1 - u_1 v_3)^2 + (u_1 v_2 - u_2 v_1)^2}\n\\]\nThe area of triangle \\(OAB\\) is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\|\n\\]\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nWe can compute the cross product:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\cdot 1 - 3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\ 3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1 \\\\ 1 \\cdot (-2) - 2 \\cdot (-3) \\end{pmatrix} = \\b