\n```python\n# Define the total area of the rectangle\ntotal_area = 8 * 4\n\n# Define the area of the triangle where x + y <= 4\ntriangle_area = 0.5 * 4 * 4\n\n# Calculate the probability\nprobability = triangle_area / total_area\n\n# Print the probability as a fraction\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nprint(Fraction(probability).limit_denominator())\n```\n```output\n1/4\n```\nThe probability that a randomly selected point $(x,y)$ within the rectangle defined by $0 \\leq x \\leq 8$ and $0 \\leq y \\leq 4$ satisfies the condition $x + y \\leq 4$ is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to use some geometric reasoning and calculus. Let's break it down step-by-step.\n\n1. **Define the Problem:**\n   - Let the speed of runner \\(A\\) be \\(v\\). Then the speed of runner \\(B\\) is \\(3v\\).\n   - Let the time elapsed be \\(t\\). After time \\(t\\), runner \\(A\\) has run a distance \\(vt\\) and runner \\(B\\) has run a distance \\(3vt\\).\n   - Let the position of \\(O\\) be the origin \\((0, 0)\\) and the track be along the x-axis. So, after time \\(t\\), runner \\(A\\) is at \\((vt, 0)\\) and runner \\(B\\) is at \\((3vt, 0)\\).\n   - The observer \\(P\\) is at \\((0, h)\\) where \\(h\\) is the height of \\(P\\) above the track. For simplicity, we can assume \\(h = 1\\).\n\n2. **Calculate the Angles:**\n   - The angle \\(\\angle APB\\) can be found using the tangent of the angle. The tangent of the angle between two lines is given by the difference in slopes divided by 1 plus the product of the slopes.\n   - The slope of \\(AP\\) is \\(\\frac{1 - 0}{0 - vt} = -\\frac{1}{vt}\\).\n   - The slope of \\(BP\\) is \\(\\frac{1 - 0}{0 - 3vt} = -\\frac{1}{3vt}\\).\n   - The tangent of \\(\\angle APB\\) is given by:\n     \\[\n     \\tan(\\angle APB) = \\left| \\frac{-\\frac{1}{vt} + \\frac{1}{3vt}}{1 + \\left(-\\frac{1}{vt}\\right)\\left(-\\frac{1}{3vt}\\right)} \\right| = \\left| \\frac{-\\frac{2}{3vt}}{1 + \\frac{1}{3v^2t^2}} \\right| = \\left| \\fra