limit_denominator()\n\nprint(angle_BAC_fraction)\n```\n```output\n270/7\n```\nThe degree measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{270}{7}}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) in the given configuration. Let's break down the problem step-by-step:\n\n1. **Understand the Geometry:**\n   - The square has four right angles (90 degrees each).\n   - The regular heptagon has interior angles of \\( \\frac{(7-2) \\cdot 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{5 \\cdot 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} \\approx 128.57^\\circ \\) each.\n\n2. **Identify the Relevant Angles:**\n   - Since \\( \\overline{AD} \\) is a common side, the angle at \\( A \\) in the heptagon is \\( \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} \\).\n   - The angle \\( \\angle BAD \\) is composed of the 90-degree angle from the square and the exterior angle of the heptagon at \\( A \\). The exterior angle of the heptagon is \\( 180^\\circ - \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\n3. **Calculate the Exterior Angle:**\n   - The exterior angle of the heptagon is \\( 180^\\circ - \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{1260^\\circ - 900^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{360^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\n4. **Determine the Angle \\( \\angle BAC \\):**\n   - Since \\( \\angle BAD \\) is composed of the 90-degree angle from the square and the exterior angle of the heptagon, we have \\( \\angle BAD = 90^\\circ + \\frac{360^\\circ}{7} \\).\n   - The angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is half of the exterior angle of the heptagon because \\( \\angle BAC \\) is the angle subtended by the same arc as the exterior angle of the heptagon at the center of the square.\n\nThus, the measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{360^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{180^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the interior angle of the heptagon\ninterior_angle_heptagon = (7 - 2) * 180 / 7\n\n# Calculate the exterior angle of the heptagon\nexterior_angle_heptagon = 180 - interior_angle_heptagon\n\n# The angle BAC is half of the exterior angle of the heptagon\nangle_BAC = exterior_angle_heptagon / 2\n\n# Express the angle as a common fraction\nangle_BAC_fraction = sp.Rational(angle_BAC).limit_denominator()\n\nprint(angle_BAC_fraction)\n```\n```output\n180/7\n```\nThe degree measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{180}{7}}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) given that a square and a regular heptagon share a common side \\( \\overline{AD} \\).\n\n1. **Understanding the Geometry**:\n    - The square has internal angles of \\(90^\\circ\\).\n    - The regular heptagon has internal angles of \\( \\frac{(7-2) \\cdot 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{5 \\cdot 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} \\approx 128.57^\\circ \\).\n\n2. **Identifying the Angle \\( \\angle BAD \\)**:\n    - Since \\( \\overline{AD} \\) is a common side, \\( \\angle BAD \\) is the internal angle of the heptagon at vertex \\( A \\), which is \\( \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\n3. **Identifying the Angle \\( \\angle CAD \\)**:\n    - Since \\( \\overline{AD} \\) is a side of the square, \\( \\angle CAD \\) is the internal angle of the square at vertex \\( A \\), which is \\( 90^\\circ \\).\n\n4. **Finding \\( \\angle BAC \\)**:\n    - The angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is the difference between \\( \\angle BAD \\) and \\( \\angle CAD \\):\n      \\[\n      \\angle BAC = \\angle BAD - \\angle CAD = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} - 90^\\circ = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} - \\frac{630^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{270^\\circ}{7}\n      \\]\n\nThus, the degree measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is \\( \\frac{270^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the calculation is accurate.\n```python\n# Calculation of the angle BAC\n# Internal angle of the heptagon\nangle_BAD = 900 / 7\n\n# Internal angle of the square\nangle_CAD = 90\n\n# Angle BAC is the difference between angle_BAD and angle_CAD\nangle_BAC = angle_BAD - angle_CAD\n\n# Representing the angle as a fraction\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nangle_BAC_fraction = Fraction(angle_BAC).limit_denominator()\n\nprint(angle_BAC_fraction)\n```\n```output\n270/7\n```\nThe degree measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{270}{7}}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to find the measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) where a square and a regular heptagon share a common side \\( \\overline{AD} \\).\n\n1. **Understanding the Geometry:**\n   - A square has internal angles of \\(90^\\circ\\).\n   - A regular heptagon has internal angles of \\(\\frac{(7-2) \\times 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{5 \\times 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7}\\).\n\n2. **Positioning the Shapes:**\n   - Let's place the square \\(ABCD\\) such that \\(A\\) and \\(D\\) are the common vertices.\n   - The heptagon will be positioned such that \\(AD\\) is one of its sides.\n\n3. **Finding the Angle \\( \\angle BAC \\):**\n   - The angle \\( \\angle BAD \\) is \\(90^\\circ\\) because it is an internal angle of the square.\n   - The angle \\( \\angle CAD \\) is the internal angle of the heptagon, which is \\(\\frac{900^\\circ}{7}\\).\n\n   The angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) can be found by subtracting \\( \\angle CAD \\) from \\( \\angle BAD \\):\n   \\[\n   \\angle BAC = \\angle BAD - \\angle CAD = 90^\\circ - \\left(\\frac{900^\\circ}{7} - 90^\\circ\\right) = 90^\\circ - \\left(\\frac{900^\\circ - 630^\\circ}{7}\\right) = 90^\\circ - \\frac{270^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{630^\\circ - 270^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{360^\\circ}{7}\n   \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the internal angle of the heptagon\nheptagon_angle = sp.Rational(900, 7)\n\n# Define the internal angle of the square\nsquare_angle = 90\n\n# Calculate the angle BAC\nangle_BAC = square_angle - (heptagon_angle - square_angle)\nangle_BAC = sp.simplify(angle_BAC)\n\nprint(angle_BAC)\n```\n```output\n360/7\n```\nThe degree measure of angle \\( \\ang