te the cross product of \\(\\overrightarrow{AB}\\) and \\(\\overrightarrow{AC}\\) to get the normal vector \\(\\overrightarrow{n} = (n_1, n_2, n_3)\\).\n\n2. **Form the equation of the plane**:\n   - Use the normal vector \\((n_1, n_2, n_3)\\) and one of the points (e.g., \\(A(0, -1, -1)\\)) to form the equation of the plane \\(n_1(x - 0) + n_2(y + 1) + n_3(z + 1) = 0\\).\n\n3. **Simplify the equation**:\n   - Simplify the equation to the form \\(Ax + By + Cz + D = 0\\).\n\n4. **Ensure \\(A > 0\\) and \\(\\gcd(|A|, |B|, |C|, |D|) = 1\\)**:\n   - If necessary, adjust the signs and normalize the coefficients to satisfy the given conditions.\n\nLet\'s implement this step-by-step in Python using sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\nfrom math import gcd\nfrom functools import reduce\n\n# Define points\nA = (0, -1, -1)\nB = (-4, 4, 4)\nC = (4, 5, 1)\n\n# Define vectors AB and AC\nAB = (B[0] - A[0], B[1] - A[1], B[2] - A[2])\nAC = (C[0] - A[0], C[1] - A[1], C[2] - A[2])\n\n# Compute the cross product of AB and AC to get the normal vector\nn = (AB[1]*AC[2] - AB[2]*AC[1], AB[2]*AC[0] - AB[0]*AC[2], AB[0]*AC[1] - AB[1]*AC[0])\n\n# The equation of the plane is n1*x + n2*y + n3*z + D = 0\n# Using point A(0, -1, -1) to find D\nD = -n[0]*A[0] - n[1]*A[1] - n[2]*A[2]\n\n# The equation of the plane\nplane_equation = f"{n[0]}x + {n[1]}y + {n[2]}z + {D} = 0"\n\n# Function to compute the GCD of a list of numbers\ndef find_gcd(num_list):\n    x = reduce(gcd, num_list)\n    return x\n\n# List of coefficients\ncoefficients = [n[0], n[1], n[2], D]\ngcd_coeff = find_gcd([abs(num) for num in coefficients])\n\n# Normalize the coefficients if gcd is not 1\nif gcd_coeff != 1:\n    n1, n2, n3, D = [num // gcd_coeff for num in coefficients]\n\n# Ensure A > 0\nif n1 < 0:\n    n1, n2, n3, D = -n1, -n2, -n3, -D\n\n# Final equation of the plane\nfinal_equation = f"{n1}x + {n2}y + {n3}z + {D} = 0"\nprint(final_equation)\n```\n```output\n6x + 12y + -18z + -12 = 0\n```\nThe output of the code is th