ined the equation \\( 3x - 2y = 26 \\). To express this in the slope-intercept form \\( y = mx + b \\), we need to solve for \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\n3x - 2y = 26\n\\]\n\nLet's isolate \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\n-2y = -3x + 26\n\\]\n\n\\[\ny = \\frac{3}{2}x - 13\n\\]\n\nThus, the equation \\( y = mx + b \\) corresponds to \\( y = \\frac{3}{2}x - 13 \\), where \\( m = \\frac{3}{2} \\) and \\( b = -13 \\).\n\nSo the ordered pair \\((m, b)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)}\n\\]", 'The line is parameterized by\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} + t \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]This means that $x = 8 + 2t$ and $y = -1 + 3t.$  Solving the first equation for $t,$ we get $t = x - 8.$  Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\\[y = -1 + 3(x - 8) = 3x - 25.\\]Thus, $m = 3$ and $b = -25,$ so the ordered pair is $\\boxed{(3,-25)}.$', "The given line is parameterized by\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} + t \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\nThis means that the line passes through the point $(8, -1)$ and has a direction vector of $\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}.$\n\nTo find the equation of the line in the form $y = mx + b$, we can use the point-slope form of the equation of a line. The slope $m$ of the line is the ratio of the $y$-component to the $x$-component of the direction vector, which is $\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nSo the equation of the line is\n\\[y - (-1) = \\frac{3}{2}(x - 8).\\]\n\nSimplifying this, we get\n\\[y + 1 = \\frac{3}{2}x - 12,\\]\n\\[y = \\frac{3}{2}x - 13.\\]\n\nThus, the ordered pair $(m, b)$ is $\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right).$\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\n# Given point and direction vector\npoint = (8, -1)\ndirection_vector = (2, 3)\n\n# Calculate the slope m\nm = direction_vector[1] / direction_vector[0]\n\n# Using the point-slope form to