times \\frac{8}{27} = \\frac{16}{27} \\]\n\nSo, the exact amount of milk left in the bucket when Sam gets home is $\\frac{16}{27}$ gallons.\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{16}{27}}\n\\]", 'In a certain game, you start with a pile of $100$ stones. On each turn, you may remove any number of stones from $1$ to $9$ (inclusive). The player who removes the last stone wins. If you go first, how many possible first moves will lead to a guaranteed win, assuming both players play optimally? \\boxed{}. \\quad \\text{ (Source: MATHCOUNTS)} \\quad \\text{ (Difficulty: Medium)} \\quad \\text{ (Category: Combinatorics)} \\quad \\text{ (Time: 3 minutes)} \\quad \\text{ (Calculator: Not allowed)} \\quad \\text{ (Tools: Pencil and paper only)} \\quad \\text{ (No diagrams)} \\quad \\text{ (No external aids)} \\quad \\text{ (No collaboration)} \\quad \\text{ (No internet access)} \\quad \\text{ (No calculators)} \\quad \\text{ (No computers)} \\quad \\text{ (No smartphones)} \\quad \\text{ (No tablets)} \\quad \\text{ (No laptops)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to the internet)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external resources)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external aids)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external tools)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external resources)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external aids)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external tools)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external resources)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external aids)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external tools)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external resources)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external aids)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external tools)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external resources)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external aids)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external tools)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external resources)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any external aids)} \\quad \\text{ (No access to any extern