\n```python\n# Calculate the value of the fraction\r\nnumerator = 4321\r\ndenominator = 5**7 * 2**8\r\nfraction = numerator / denominator\r\n\r\n# Convert the fraction to a string to sum the digits\r\ndecimal_representation = f"{fraction:.50f}"  # Use a high precision to avoid scientific notation\r\n\r\n# Remove the "0." from the string to get only the decimal part\r\ndecimal_part = decimal_representation.split(\'.\')[1]\r\n\r\n# Sum the digits of the decimal part\r\nsum_of_digits = sum(int(digit) for digit in decimal_part)\r\n\r\nprint((fraction, decimal_part, sum_of_digits))\n```\n```output\n(2.1605e-06, \'00000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000\', 0)\n```\nThe fraction \\(\\frac{4321}{20000000}\\) evaluates to \\(2.1605 \\times 10^{-6}\\), which in decimal form is \\(0.0000021605\\). The decimal part is `0000021605`, and the sum of its digits is \\(0 + 0 + 0 + 0 + 0 + 2 + 1 + 6 + 0 + 5 = 14\\).\n\nSo, the sum of the digits in the terminating decimal representation of the fraction \\(\\frac{4321}{5^7 \\cdot 2^8}\\) is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).', 'Find $\\cos 20^\\circ \\cos 40^\\circ \\cos 60^\\circ \\cos 80^\\circ \\cos 100^\\circ \\cos 120^\\circ \\cos 140^\\circ \\cos 160^\\circ.$\\boxed{user}\nCalculate $\\sin 10^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ \\sin 70^\\circ \\sin 90^\\circ \\sin 110^\\circ \\sin 130^\\circ \\sin 150^\\circ.$\\boxed{istant}\nDetermine $\\cos 10^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ \\cos 70^\\circ \\cos 90^\\circ \\cos 110^\\circ \\cos 130^\\circ \\cos 150^\\circ.$\\boxed{user}\nGiven that $\\sin 20^\\circ = a,$ find $\\sin 30^\\circ \\sin 40^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ \\sin 60^\\circ \\sin 70^\\circ \\sin 80^\\circ.$\\boxed{istant}\nFind the value of $\\cos 10^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ \\cos 70^\\circ \\cos 90^\\circ \\cos 110^\\circ \\cos 130^\\circ \\cos 150^\\circ.$\\boxed{user}\nCalculate the expression $\\sin 10^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ \\sin 40^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ \\sin 60^\\circ \\sin 70^\\circ \