 by the formula:\n\\[d = \\frac{|ax + by + cz + d|}{\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2 + c^2}}.\\]\n\nFor the plane $x - z = 0$, the distance $d_1$ is:\n\\[d_1 = \\frac{|x - z|}{\\sqrt{1^2 + 0^2 + (-1)^2}} = \\frac{|x - z|}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\]\n\nFor the plane $x - 2y + z = 0$, the distance $d_2$ is:\n\\[d_2 = \\frac{|x - 2y + z|}{\\sqrt{1^2 + (-2)^2 + 1^2}} = \\frac{|x - 2y + z|}{\\sqrt{6}}.\\]\n\nFor the plane $x + y + z = 0$, the distance $d_3$ is:\n\\[d_3 = \\frac{|x + y + z|}{\\sqrt{1^2 + 1^2 + 1^2}} = \\frac{|x + y + z|}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\]\n\nThe equation $d_1^2 + d_2^2 + d_3^2 = 36$ can be written as:\n\\[\\left(\\frac{|x - z|}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{|x - 2y + z|}{\\sqrt{6}}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{|x + y + z|}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)^2 = 36.\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\\frac{(x - z)^2}{2} + \\frac{(x - 2y + z)^2}{6} + \\frac{(x + y + z)^2}{3} = 36.\\]\n\nTo find the volume of the region $S$, we need to recognize that this equation represents an ellipsoid. The standard form of an ellipsoid is:\n\\[\\frac{x^2}{a^2} + \\frac{y^2}{b^2} + \\frac{z^2}{c^2} = 1.\\]\n\nTo transform our equation into the standard form, we need to find the values of $a$, $b$, and $c$. By comparing the coefficients, we can see that:\n\\[\\frac{(x - z)^2}{2} + \\frac{(x - 2y + z)^2}{6} + \\frac{(x + y + z)^2}{3} = 36\\]\ncan be rewritten as:\n\\[\\frac{(x - z)^2}{72} + \\frac{(x - 2y + z)^2}{216} + \\frac{(x + y + z)^2}{108} = 1.\\]\n\nThis is the standard form of an ellipsoid with semi-axes lengths $a = \\sqrt{72}$, $b = \\sqrt{216}$, and $c = \\sqrt{108}$. The volume $V$ of an ellipsoid with semi-axes lengths $a$, $b$, and $c$ is given by:\n\\[V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi abc.\\]\n\nSubstituting the values of $a$, $b$, and $c$, we get:\n\\[V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\sqrt{72} \\sqrt{216} \\sqrt{108}.\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Semi-axes lengths\na = math.sqrt(72)\nb = math.sqrt(216)\nc = math.sqrt(108)\n\n# Volume of the ellipsoid\nvolume = (4/3) 