t and width of the first parallelogram:**\n   - The height of the parallelogram is the vertical distance between the lines $y = ax + c$ and $y = ax + d$, which is $|d - c|$.\n   - The width of the parallelogram is the horizontal distance between the intersections of the lines $y = ax + c$ and $y = bx + c$, and $y = ax + d$ and $y = bx + d$. This distance is given by the difference in the x-coordinates of the intersections, which is $\\left| \\frac{c - d}{a - b} \\right|$.\n   - The area of the first parallelogram is then $|d - c| \\cdot \\left| \\frac{c - d}{a - b} \\right| = 18$.\n\n2. **Calculate the height and width of the second parallelogram:**\n   - The height of the parallelogram is the vertical distance between the lines $y = ax + c$ and $y = ax - d$, which is $|c + d|$.\n   - The width of the parallelogram is the horizontal distance between the intersections of the lines $y = ax + c$ and $y = bx + c$, and $y = ax - d$ and $y = bx - d$. This distance is given by the difference in the x-coordinates of the intersections, which is $\\left| \\frac{c + d}{a - b} \\right|$.\n   - The area of the second parallelogram is then $|c + d| \\cdot \\left| \\frac{c + d}{a - b} \\right| = 72$.\n\nWe can now set up the equations:\n\\[ |d - c| \\cdot \\left| \\frac{c - d}{a - b} \\right| = 18 \\]\n\\[ |c + d| \\cdot \\left| \\frac{c + d}{a - b} \\right| = 72 \\]\n\nSince $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$ are positive integers, we can simplify these equations to:\n\\[ (d - c) \\cdot \\frac{d - c}{a - b} = 18 \\]\n\\[ (c + d) \\cdot \\frac{c + d}{a - b} = 72 \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ \\frac{(d - c)^2}{a - b} = 18 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{(c + d)^2}{a - b} = 72 \\]\n\nFrom these equations, we can solve for $a - b$:\n\\[ (d - c)^2 = 18(a - b) \\]\n\\[ (c + d)^2 = 72(a - b) \\]\n\nWe can now iterate through possible values of $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$ to find the smallest possible value of $a + b + c + d$. Let's write the code to find the solution.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Function to find the