rray([-2, 1, -1])\n\n# Compute the vectors BA and BC\nBA = A - B\nBC = C - B\n\n# Compute the dot product of BA and BC\ndot_product = np.dot(BA, BC)\n\n# Compute the magnitudes of BA and BC\nmagnitude_BA = np.linalg.norm(BA)\nmagnitude_BC = np.linalg.norm(BC)\n\n# Compute the cosine of the angle\ncos_theta = dot_product / (magnitude_BA * magnitude_BC)\n\n# Compute the angle in degrees\nangle_degrees = np.degrees(np.arccos(cos_theta))\nprint(angle_degrees)\n```\n```output\n120.00000000000001\n```\nThe computed angle is $120^\\circ$. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{120}\n\\]", "To find the angle $\\angle ABC$, we need to use the dot product formula for vectors. The dot product of two vectors $\\vec{u}$ and $\\vec{v}$ is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\vec{u} \\cdot \\vec{v} = \\|\\vec{u}\\| \\|\\vec{v}\\| \\cos(\\theta)\n\\]\n\nwhere $\\theta$ is the angle between the vectors $\\vec{u}$ and $\\vec{v}$. Rearranging for $\\cos(\\theta)$, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{\\vec{u} \\cdot \\vec{v}}{\\|\\vec{u}\\| \\|\\vec{v}\\|}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to find the vectors $\\vec{BA}$ and $\\vec{BC}$. These vectors are given by:\n\n\\[\n\\vec{BA} = A - B = (1 - 3, -11 - (-4), 2 - 1) = (-2, -7, 1)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\vec{BC} = C - B = (-2 - 3, 1 - (-4), -1 - 1) = (-5, 5, -2)\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute the dot product of $\\vec{BA}$ and $\\vec{BC}$:\n\n\\[\n\\vec{BA} \\cdot \\vec{BC} = (-2)(-5) + (-7)(5) + (1)(-2) = 10 - 35 - 2 = -27\n\\]\n\nThen, we compute the magnitudes of $\\vec{BA}$ and $\\vec{BC}$:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\vec{BA}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-7)^2 + 1^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 49 + 1} = \\sqrt{54} = 3\\sqrt{6}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\|\\vec{BC}\\| = \\sqrt{(-5)^2 + 5^2 + (-2)^2} = \\sqrt{25 + 25 + 4} = \\sqrt{54} = 3\\sqrt{6}\n\\]\n\nNow we can find $\\cos(\\theta)$:\n\n\\[\n\\cos(\\theta) = \\frac{\\vec{BA} \\cdot \\vec{BC}}{\\|\\vec{BA}\\| \\|\\vec{BC}\\|} = \\frac{-27}{(3\\sqrt{6})(3\\sqrt{6})} = \\frac{-27}{54} = -\\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nSo, $\\theta = \\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\r