 Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the sum of the first 10 natural numbers\nn = 10\nsum_n = n * (n + 1) // 2\n\n# Find the remainder when this sum is divided by 9\nremainder = sum_n % 9\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n1\n```\nThe remainder when the sum of the first 10 natural numbers (which is 55) is divided by 9 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).", "What is the remainder when $1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\dots + 9 + 10 + 11$ is divided by 9? Shayna is planning a birthday party and wants to make sure she has enough cupcakes for all her friends. If she invites 10 friends and each friend can eat 2 cupcakes, how many cupcakes does she need to bake? Shayna knows she can only bake 15 cupcakes at a time. How many times does she need to bake to have enough cupcakes for her party? Shayna wants to make sure she has enough cupcakes for her party. She knows that each of her 10 friends will eat 2 cupcakes. To find out how many cupcakes she needs in total, she multiplies the number of friends by the number of cupcakes each friend will eat:\n10 friends × 2 cupcakes per friend = 20 cupcakes\nShayna knows she can only bake 15 cupcakes at a time. To find out how many times she needs to bake to have enough cupcakes, she divides the total number of cupcakes by the number of cupcakes she can bake at a time:\n20 cupcakes ÷ 15 cupcakes per batch = 1.33 batches\nSince Shayna can't bake a fraction of a batch, she needs to round up to the nearest whole number. Therefore, she needs to bake 2 batches of cupcakes to have enough for her party.", "To find the remainder when the sum of the first 10 natural numbers is divided by 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the sum of the first 10 natural numbers.\n2. Find the remainder when this sum is divided by 9.\n\nThe sum of the first \\( n \\) natural numbers is given by the formula:\n\\[ S = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\]\n\nFor \\( n = 10 \\):\n\\[ S = \\frac{10 \\times 11}{2} = 55 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 55 is divided by 9. We can do this usi