ues for \\( k \\).\n\nTherefore, there are 21 real values of \\( x \\) for which \\(\\sqrt{120 - \\sqrt{x}}\\) is an integer.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the range of k values\nk_min = -int(math.sqrt(120))\nk_max = int(math.sqrt(120))\n\n# The number of integer values of k from k_min to k_max inclusive\nnum_real_values = k_max - k_min + 1\nprint(num_real_values)\n```\n```output\n21\n```\nThe number of real values of \\( x \\) for which \\(\\sqrt{120 - \\sqrt{x}}\\) is an integer is \\(\\boxed{21}\\).", 'A rectangular box has integer side lengths in the ratio $1: 3: 4$. Which of the following could be the volume of the box?  \\textbf{(A)} 48\\qquad\\textbf{(B)} 56\\qquad\\textbf{(C)} 64\\qquad\\textbf{(D)} 96\\qquad\\textbf{(E)} 144\\qquad \\boxed{}.', 'In the addition problem below $A, B, C,$ and $D$ are different digits. What is $A+B?$ \\[\\begin{array}{c@{}c@{\\;}c@{}c@{}c@{}c}& & & A & B & A\\\\ &+& & C & D & \\\\ \\cline{2-6}& & & D & B & C\\\\ \\end{array}\\] \\textbf{(A) }2\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }4\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }7\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }8\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }9$http://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/2003_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\n \\textbf{Assistant}\n A base-$b$ number $x_{b}$ is converted to base-10 as follows: $x_{b} = a_{n}b^{n} + a_{n-1}b^{n-1} + \\ldots + a_{1}b^{1} + a_{0}b^{0}$, where $a_{n}, a_{n-1}, \\ldots, a_{1}, a_{0}$ are digits in base $b$. For what base $b$ is the base-$b$ number $235_{b} = 111110_{2}$? \\textbf{(A) }3\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }4\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }5\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }6\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }7$http://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\n \\textbf{Assistant}\n A set of tiles numbered 1 through 100 is modified repeatedly by the following operation: remove all tiles numbered with a perfect square , and renumber the remaining tiles consecutively starting with 1. How many times must the operation be performed to reduce the number of tiles in th