thbf{a}_1 = \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix}.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the cross product \\(\\mathbf{n} = \\mathbf{b}_1 \\times \\mathbf{c}\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{n} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} \\times \\begin{pmatrix} -8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 2 & -9 & -2 \\\\ -8 & 7 & 5 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i}(-9 \\cdot 5 - (-2) \\cdot 7) - \\mathbf{j}(2 \\cdot 5 - (-2) \\cdot (-8)) + \\mathbf{k}(2 \\cdot 7 - (-9) \\cdot (-8)) = \\mathbf{i}(-45 + 14) - \\mathbf{j}(10 - 16) + \\mathbf{k}(14 - 72) = \\begin{pmatrix} -31 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -58 \\end{pmatrix}.\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the magnitude of \\(\\mathbf{n}\\):**\n   \\[\n   |\\mathbf{n}| = \\sqrt{(-31)^2 + 6^2 + (-58)^2} = \\sqrt{961 + 36 + 3364} = \\sqrt{4361}.\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{n} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a}_2 - \\mathbf{a}_1)\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{n} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a}_2 - \\mathbf{a}_1) = \\begin{pmatrix} -31 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -58 \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} -8 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = (-31) \\cdot (-8) + 6 \\cdot 7 + (-58) \\cdot 5 = 2", "To find the distance between two parallel lines, we can use the following approach:\n\n1. **Identify the parametric equations of the lines:**\n   - Line 1: \\(\\mathbf{r}_1(t) = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} + t \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\)\n   - Line 2: \\(\\mathbf{r}_2(u) = \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\end{pmatrix} + u \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -4 \\end{pmatrix}\\)\n\n2. **Find a vector that connects a point on Line 1 to a point on Line 2:**\n   - Let's choose the points \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) on Line 1 and \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 6 \\end{pmatrix}\\) on Line 2.\n   - The vector \\(\\mathbf{d}\\) 