ituting \\( r = 4 \\) back into the original equation to ensure it holds true.\n```python\n# Define the value of r\nr = 4\n\n# Calculate the left-hand side of the original equation\nlhs = (6 * r**2 - 19 * r - 7) / (2 * r - 7)\n\n# Calculate the right-hand side of the original equation\nrhs = 4 * r - 3\n\n# Check if the left-hand side equals the right-hand side\nprint((lhs, rhs, lhs == rhs))\n```", "To solve the equation \\(\\frac{6r^2 - 19r - 7}{2r - 7} = 4r - 3\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. First, we'll eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides of the equation by \\(2r - 7\\):\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 = (4r - 3)(2r - 7).\\]\n\n2. Next, we'll expand the right-hand side:\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 28r - 6r + 21.\\]\n\n3. Simplify the right-hand side:\n\\[6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 34r + 21.\\]\n\n4. Move all terms to one side of the equation to set it to zero:\n\\[0 = 8r^2 - 34r + 21 - 6r^2 + 19r + 7.\\]\n\n5. Combine like terms:\n\\[0 = 2r^2 - 15r + 28.\\]\n\n6. Now we have a standard quadratic equation:\n\\[2r^2 - 15r + 28 = 0.\\]\n\n7. We'll solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\(r = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 2\\), \\(b = -15\\), and \\(c = 28\\):\n\\[r = \\frac{-(-15) \\pm \\sqrt{(-15)^2 - 4 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 28}}{2 \\cdot 2} = \\frac{15 \\pm \\sqrt{225 - 224}}{4} = \\frac{15 \\pm \\sqrt{1}}{4} = \\frac{15 \\pm 1}{4}.\\]\n\n8. This gives us two solutions:\n\\[r = \\frac{16}{4} = 4 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad r = \\frac{14}{4} = \\frac{7}{2}.\\]\n\n9. We need to check if these solutions are valid by substituting them back into the original equation. We'll start with \\(r = 4\\):\n\\[\\frac{6(4)^2 - 19(4) - 7}{2(4) - 7} = \\frac{6 \\cdot 16 - 76 - 7}{8 - 7} = \\frac{96 - 76 - 7}{1} = \\frac{13}{1} = 13,\\]\nand\n\\[4(4) - 3 = 16 - 3 = 13.\\]\nSince both sides are equal, \\(r = 4\\) is a valid solution.\n\n10. Now we'll check \\(r = \\frac{7}{2}\\):\n\\[\\frac{6\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2 - 19\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) - 7}{2\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) - 7} = \\frac{6 \\cdot \\frac{49}{4} - \\frac{133}{2} - 7}{7 - 7} = \\frac{\\frac{294}{4} - \\frac{133}{2} - 7}{0} = \\frac{\\frac{147}{2} - \\frac{133}{2} - 7}{0} = \\frac{7 - 7}{0} = \\frac{0}{0},\\]\nwhich is undefined. Therefore, \\(r = \\frac{7}{2}\\) is not a valid solution.\n\nSo the only valid solution is \\(r = 4\\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).", 'Given that $a$ and $b$ are nonzero constants such that $$\\frac{ax+b}{x-3} = k + \\frac{r}{x-3},$$ where $k$ and $r$ are constants, find the ordered pair $(k,r)$ in terms of $a$ and $b$. \\boxed{} \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\rangle\n| \\langle \\r