en polynomial equation \\(z^4 + 4z^3i - 6z^2 - 4zi - i = 0\\). The roots of this polynomial will be the vertices of the convex polygon in the complex plane. Once we have the roots, we can determine the shape and area of the polygon.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the polynomial. We can use Python to find the roots of the polynomial \\(z^4 + 4z^3i - 6z^2 - 4zi - i = 0\\).\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Define the coefficients of the polynomial z^4 + 4z^3i - 6z^2 - 4zi - i = 0\ncoefficients = [1, 4j, -6, -4j, -1j]\n\n# Find the roots of the polynomial\nroots = np.roots(coefficients)\nprint(roots)\n```\n```output\n[ 1.18619952e-16+1.60173334j -1.60173334e+00+1.18619952e-16j\n -7.24536788e-17+1.j           1.02824263e-16+0.43844719j]\n```\nThe roots of the polynomial \\(z^4 + 4z^3i - 6z^2 - 4zi - i = 0\\) are approximately:\n\\[1.60173334i,\\]\n\\[-1.60173334 + 1.18619952 \\times 10^{-16}i,\\]\n\\[i,\\]\n\\[0.43844719i.\\]\n\nThese roots are essentially \\(1.60173334i\\), \\(-1.60173334\\), \\(i\\), and \\(0.43844719i\\). These roots form a rectangle in the complex plane with vertices at \\((0, 1.60173334)\\), \\((-1.60173334, 0)\\), \\((0, 1)\\), and \\((0, 0.43844719)\\).\n\nThe length of the vertical side of the rectangle is \\(1.60173334 - 0.43844719 = 1.16328615\\), and the length of the horizontal side is \\(1.60173334\\).\n\nThe area of the rectangle is given by the product of its side lengths:\n\\[ \\text{Area} = 1.60173334 \\times 1.16328615. \\]\n\nWe can calculate this product to get the area. Let's do this calculation in Python.\n\n```python\n# Calculate the area of the rectangle\nvertical_side = 1.60173334 - 0.43844719\nhorizontal_side = 1.60173334\narea = vertical_side * horizontal_side\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n1.863389981258914\n```\nThe area of the rectangle is approximately \\(1.863389981258914\\). To express this area in the form \\(p^{a/b}\\), where \\(p\\) is a prime number, \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are relatively prime positive integers, w