nto manageable steps:\n\n1. **Find the roots of the polynomial equation.**\n2. **Determine the vertices of the polygon formed by these roots.**\n3. **Calculate the area of the polygon.**\n4. **Express the area in the form \\(p^{a/b}\\) and find \\(a + b + p\\).**\n\nWe will use Python and SymPy to find the roots of the polynomial and then calculate the area of the polygon formed by these roots.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nz = sp.symbols('z')\n\n# Define the polynomial equation\npolynomial = z**4 + 4*z**3*sp.I - 6*z**2 - 4*z*sp.I - sp.I\n\n# Find the roots of the polynomial\nroots = sp.solve(polynomial, z)\n\n# Convert the roots to a list of complex numbers\nroots = [complex(root.evalf()) for root in roots]\n\n# Function to calculate the area of a polygon given its vertices\ndef polygon_area(vertices):\n    n = len(vertices)\n    area = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        j = (i + 1) % n\n        area += vertices[i].real * vertices[j].imag\n        area -= vertices[j].real * vertices[i].imag\n    area = abs(area) / 2.0\n    return area\n\n# Calculate the area of the polygon formed by the roots\narea = polygon_area(roots)\n\n# Simplify the area to the form p^(a/b)\narea_simplified = sp.simplify(area)\n\n# Extract p, a, b from the simplified area\np = sp.primefactors(area_simplified)[0]\na = sp.numer(area_simplified)\nb = sp.denom(area_simplified)\n\n# Calculate a + b + p\nresult = a + b + p\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\nIndexError: list index out of range\n```\nIt looks like there was an issue with the code. The error indicates that the list of prime factors of the simplified area is empty, which suggests that the area might not have been simplified correctly or might not have been in the expected form.\n\nLet's re-evaluate the steps and ensure that we correctly find the roots and calculate the area of the polygon. We'll also make sure to handle the simplification of the area properly.\n\nHere's the revised code:\n\n```python\nimport sy