 polygon in the complex plane\nvertices = roots\n\n# Function to calculate the area of the convex polygon\ndef polygon_area(vertices):\n    n = len(vertices)\n    area = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        x1, y1 = vertices[i].real, vertices[i].imag\n        x2, y2 = vertices[(i + 1) % n].real, vertices[(i + 1) % n].imag\n        area += x1 * y2 - x2 * y1\n    return abs(area) / 2\n\n# Calculate the area of the convex polygon\narea = polygon_area(vertices)\nprint((roots, area))\n```\n```output\n(array([-2.67706534e+00+1.67706534j,  2.67706534e+00-1.67706534j,\n       -1.00000000e+00+1.00000000e+00j, -1.57009246e-16-1.00000000e+00j]), 0.0)\n```\nThe roots of the polynomial \\(z^4 + 4z^3i - 6z^2 - 4zi - i = 0\\) are approximately:\n\\[\n-2.677 + 1.677i, \\quad 2.677 - 1.677i, \\quad -1 + i, \\quad -1 - i\n\\]\nThese roots form a convex polygon in the complex plane. However, the area calculated is 0. This suggests that the roots are collinear or form a degenerate polygon. Let\'s verify this by checking if the roots are indeed collinear.\n\nWe can check the collinearity by verifying if the area of the triangle formed by any three of the roots is zero. If the area is zero, then the roots are collinear.\n\nLet\'s check the collinearity of the roots.\n```python\n# Function to calculate the area of the triangle formed by three points in the complex plane\ndef triangle_area(z1, z2, z3):\n    x1, y1 = z1.real, z1.imag\n    x2, y2 = z2.real, z2.imag\n    x3, y3 = z3.real, z3.imag\n    return abs(x1*(y2 - y3) + x2*(y3 - y1) + x3*(y1 - y2)) / 2\n\n# Check the collinearity of the roots\narea_triangle_1 = triangle_area(vertices[0], vertices[1], vertices[2])\narea_triangle_2 = triangle_area(vertices[0], vertices[1], vertices[3])\narea_triangle_3 = triangle_area(vertices[0], vertices[2], vertices[3])\narea_triangle_4 = triangle_area(vertices[1], vertices[2], vertices[3])\n\nprint((area_triangle_1, area_triangle_2, area_triangle_3, area_triangle_4))\n```\n```output\nNameError: name \'