ate the total number of stamps in the 70s\ntotal_stamps_70s = num_brazil_70s + num_france_70s + num_peru_70s +', '\\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|c|c|}\n\\hline \\textbf{Country} & \\textbf{50\'s} & \\textbf{60\'s} & \\textbf{70\'s} & \\textbf{80\'s} \\\\\n\\hline\nBrazil & 4 & 7 & 12 & 8 \\\\\n\\hline\nFrance & 6 & 4 & 7 & 8 \\\\\n\\hline\nPeru & 6 & 4 & 12 & 15 \\\\\n\\hline\nSpain & 5 & 9 & 13 & 10 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{tabular}\n\nAssistant: To determine the average price of Juan\'s stamps from the 1970s, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of stamps from the 1970s for each country.\n2. Calculate the total cost for each decade by multiplying the number of stamps by the price per stamp.\n3. Sum the total costs for the 1970s.\n4. Calculate the total number of stamps from the 1970s.\n5. Compute the average price per stamp by dividing the total cost by the total number of stamps.\n\nLet\'s extract the relevant data from the table:\n\n- Brazil: 12 stamps in the 1970s\n- France: 7 stamps in the 1970s\n- Peru: 12 stamps in the 1970s\n- Spain: 13 stamps in the 1970s\n\nThe prices per stamp are:\n- Brazil: 6 cents\n- France: 4 cents\n- Peru: 4 cents\n- Spain: 5 cents\n\nNow, let\'s calculate the total cost and the average price using Python.\n```python\n# Number of stamps in the 1970s for each country\nstamps_1970s = {\n    "Brazil": 12,\n    "France": 7,\n    "Peru": 12,\n    "Spain": 13\n}\n\n# Prices per stamp\nprices = {\n    "Brazil": 6,\n    "France": 4,\n    "Peru": 4,\n    "Spain": 5\n}\n\n# Calculate the total cost for the 1970s\ntotal_cost = sum(stamps_1970s[country] * prices[country] for country in stamps_1970s)\ntotal_stamps = sum(stamps_1970s.values())\n\n# Calculate the average price per stamp\naverage_price = total_cost / total_stamps\n\n# Round to the nearest tenth of a cent\naverage_price_rounded = round(average_price, 1)\nprint(average_price_rounded)\n```\n```output\n4.8\n```\nThe average price of Juan\'s 1970s stamps is \\(\\boxed{4.8}\\) c