culate the Area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\):**\n   - Let the height of the trapezoid be \\(h\\) and the length of \\(AD\\) be \\(a\\) and \\(BC\\) be \\(b\\).\n   - The area of the trapezoid \\(ABCD\\) is given by \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times (AD + BC) \\times h = 42\\).\n   - Since \\(AC\\) bisects \\(\\angle BAD\\), the height \\(h\\) of the trapezoid is the same as the height of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) and \\(\\triangle ABC\\).\n   - The area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) is \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times AD \\times h\\).\n   - The area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times BC \\times h\\).\n   - Since the total area of the trapezoid is 42, we have \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times (a + b) \\times h = 42\\).\n\n4. **Use Similarity:**\n   - Since \\(\\triangle ACD \\sim \\triangle ABC\\), the ratio of their areas is the square of the ratio of their corresponding sides. But since \\(AC\\) is the common side, the ratio of the areas is actually the ratio of the bases \\(AD\\) and \\(BC\\).\n   - Let the area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) be \\(x\\). Then the area of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is \\(42 - x\\).\n   - Since the triangles are similar and share the same height, the ratio of their areas is the same as the ratio of their bases. So, \\(\\frac{x}{42 - x} = \\frac{a}{b}\\).\n\n5. **Solve for the Area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\):**\n   - Since \\(AC\\) bisects \\(\\angle BAD\\) and \\(AC \\perp CD\\), the triangles are similar in such a way that the ratio of their areas is the same as the ratio of their bases. This means that the area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) is half of the area of the trapezoid because the height and the base \\(AD\\) are effectively splitting the trapezoid into two equal parts in terms of area.\n   - Therefore, the area of \\(\\triangle ACD\\) is \\(\\frac{42}{2} = 21\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the area of the trapezoid\ntotal_area = 42\n\n# Since AC bisects angle BAD and AC is perpendicular to CD, the area of tria