urther, let's evaluate it at specific points.\n\n1. Evaluate at \\(x = a\\):\n\\[ (a - b)(a - c)(b - c) + (a - a)(a - c)(a - b) + (a - a)(a - b)(c - a) = (a - b)(a - c)(b - c). \\]\n\n2. Evaluate at \\(x = b\\):\n\\[ (b - b)(b - c)(b - c) + (b - a)(b - c)(a - b) + (b - a)(b - b)(c - a) = (b - a)(b - c)(a - b) = -(a - b)^2(b - c). \\]\n\n3. Evaluate at \\(x = c\\):\n\\[ (c - b)(c - c)(b - c) + (c - a)(c - c)(a - b) + (c - a)(c - b)(c - a) = (c - a)(c - b)(c - a) = (c - a)^2(c - b). \\]\n\nSince the polynomial in the numerator is zero at \\(x = a\\), \\(x = b\\), and \\(x = c\\), it must be divisible by \\((x - a)(x - b)(x - c)\\). However, since the numerator is a polynomial of degree at most 2, it must be identically zero. Therefore, the entire polynomial \\( p(x) \\) simplifies to 1.\n\nSo, the degree of the polynomial \\( p(x) \\) is 0.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, simplify\r\n\r\n# Define the variables\r\nx, a, b, c = symbols('x a b c')\r\n\r\n# Define the polynomial p(x)\r\np_x = ((x - b)*(x - c))/((a - b)*(a - c)) + ((x - a)*(x - c))/((b - a)*(b - c)) + ((x - a)*(x - b))/((c - a)*(c - b))\r\n\r\n# Simplify the polynomial\r\nsimplified_p_x = simplify(p_x)\r\nprint(simplified_p_x)\n```\n```output\n1\n```\nThe simplified form of the polynomial \\( p(x) \\) is \\( 1 \\), which is a constant polynomial of degree 0. Therefore, the degree of the polynomial \\( p(x) \\) is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To find the degree of the polynomial \\( p(x) \\), we need to analyze the expression:\n\n\\[ p(x) = \\frac{(x - b)(x - c)}{(a - b)(a - c)} + \\frac{(x - a)(x - c)}{(b - a)(b - c)} + \\frac{(x - a)(x - b)}{(c - a)(c - b)}. \\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify each term individually. Each term is a quadratic polynomial divided by a constant. The degree of each term is the degree of the numerator minus the degree of the denominator. Since the numerator of each term is a quadratic polynomial (degree 2) and the