meters = length_km * 1000  # meters\n\nprint(length_meters)\n```', "To determine the length of the hallway, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the speed of the robot.\n2. Convert the time it takes to travel the length of the hallway from seconds to hours.\n3. Use the speed and the time to calculate the length of the hallway.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the speed of the robot. The robot travels 1 kilometer in 2.5 hours. So, the speed of the robot is:\n\\[ \\text{Speed} = \\frac{1 \\text{ km}}{2.5 \\text{ hours}} = 0.4 \\text{ km/h} \\]\n\nNext, we need to convert 90 seconds into hours. Since there are 3600 seconds in an hour:\n\\[ 90 \\text{ seconds} = \\frac{90}{3600} \\text{ hours} = 0.025 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNow, we can use the speed and the time to calculate the length of the hallway. The length of the hallway is the product of the speed of the robot and the time it takes to travel that length:\n\\[ \\text{Length of the hallway} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 0.4 \\text{ km/h} \\times 0.025 \\text{ hours} = 0.01 \\text{ km} \\]\n\nSince 1 kilometer is equal to 1000 meters, the length of the hallway in meters is:\n\\[ 0.01 \\text{ km} \\times 1000 \\text{ m/km} = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given data\ndistance_km = 1  # distance in kilometers\ntime_hours = 2.5  # time in hours\ntime_seconds = 90  # time in seconds\n\n# Calculate the speed of the robot in km/h\nspeed_km_per_hour = distance_km / time_hours\n\n# Convert time from seconds to hours\ntime_hours_for_hallway = time_seconds / 3600\n\n# Calculate the length of the hallway in kilometers\nlength_km = speed_km_per_hour * time_hours_for_hallway\n\n# Convert the length from kilometers to meters\nlength_meters = length_km * 1000\n\nprint(length_meters)\n```\n```output\n10.0\n```\nThe length of the hallway is \\(\\boxed{10}\\) meters.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the speed of the robot and then use that speed to find the length