ngth of the hallway:\n\\[ \\text{Length of the hallway} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 400 \\text{ meters/hour} \\times \\frac{1}{40} \\text{ hours} = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nSo, the length of the hallway is 10 meters. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed of the robot in meters per hour\nspeed_meters_per_hour = 1000 / 2.5\n\n# Convert 90 seconds to hours\ntime_hours = 90 / 3600\n\n# Calculate the length of the hallway\nlength_of_hallway = speed_meters_per_hour * time_hours\nprint(length_of_hallway)\n```\n```output\n10.0\n```\nThe length of the hallway is \\(\\boxed{10}\\) meters.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the speed of the robot and then use that speed to find the length of the hallway.\n\n1. First, we need to calculate the speed of the robot. The robot travels 1 kilometer in 2.5 hours. Since speed is distance divided by time, the speed of the robot is:\n\\[ \\text{Speed} = \\frac{1 \\text{ km}}{2.5 \\text{ hours}} = 0.4 \\text{ km/h} \\]\n\n2. Next, we need to convert the time it takes to travel the length of the hallway from seconds to hours. There are 3600 seconds in an hour, so 90 seconds is:\n\\[ \\text{Time} = \\frac{90 \\text{ seconds}}{3600 \\text{ seconds/hour}} = 0.025 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\n3. Now we can use the speed of the robot to find the length of the hallway. The length of the hallway is the speed of the robot multiplied by the time it takes to travel that length:\n\\[ \\text{Length of hallway} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 0.4 \\text{ km/h} \\times 0.025 \\text{ hours} = 0.01 \\text{ km} \\]\n\n4. Finally, we need to convert the length of the hallway from kilometers to meters. Since there are 1000 meters in a kilometer, the length of the hallway is:\n\\[ \\text{Length of hallway} = 0.01 \\text{ km} \\times 1000 \\text{ meters/km} = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed of the robot in km/h\nspeed_km_per_h = 1 / 2.5  # 1 km / 