eft( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x = \\left( \\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x$ will be a positive fraction less than 1 for $x > 0$. The floor of this value will be 0 for all $x > 0$ since $\\left( \\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x < 1$ for all $x > 0$. Therefore, $f(x) = 0$ for all even integer values of $x > 0$.\n\nFor odd integer values of $x$, the value $\\left( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x = -\\left( \\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x$ will be a negative fraction. The floor of a negative fraction is the next lower integer, which will be -1 for all odd integer values of $x > 0$ since $-1 < -\\left( \\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x < 0$ for all $x > 0$. Therefore, $f(x) = -1$ for all odd integer values of $x > 0$.\n\nFinally, for $x = 0$, we have $\\left( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^0 = 1$, so $f(0) = \\left\\lfloor 1 \\right\\rfloor = 1$.\n\nTherefore, the distinct values in the range of $f(x)$ are $1, 0, -1$. The number of distinct values is 3.\n\nLet's confirm this reasoning with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\ndef f(x):\n    return math.floor((-5/8)**x)\n\n# We will check the values of f(x) for a range of x values\ndistinct_values = set()\nfor x in range(100):  # Checking for the first 100 values of x\n    distinct_values.add(f(x))\n\nprint((distinct_values, len(distinct_values)))\n```\n```output\n({0, 1, -1}, 3)\n```\nThe distinct values in the range of $f(x)$ are $1, 0, -1$. Therefore, the number of distinct values in the range of $f(x)$ is $\\boxed{3}$.\n\nIn the figure below, a 3-inch by 3-inch square adjoins a 10-inch by 10-inch square. A 2-inch by 2-inch square is placed inside the shaded region, touching one vertex of the larger square and two sides of the smaller square. What is the area of the remaining shaded region?\nTo solve the problem, we need to calculate the area of the shaded region after placing the 2-inch by 2-inch square inside the larger shaded region. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the larger square**:\n   The larger square has a side length of 10 inc