thon code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Define the terms\r\nterm1 = 5 / math.sqrt(80)\r\nterm2 = math.sqrt(845) / 9\r\nterm3 = math.sqrt(45)\r\n\r\n# Sum of the terms\r\nnumerator = term1 + term2 + term3\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nresult = math.sqrt(numerator / math.sqrt(5))\r\n\r\n# Simplified fraction\r\nsimplified_fraction = result\r\nprint(simplified_fraction)\n```", "To simplify the given expression, we will break it down step by step. The expression we need to simplify is:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}+\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}+\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify the terms inside the square root in the numerator:\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n\\[\n\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\dfrac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n\\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nNow we can combine these simplified terms:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nTo combine these terms, we need a common denominator. The common denominator for 4, 9, and 1 is 36:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} = \\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} = \\dfrac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad 3\\sqrt{5} = \\dfrac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5} = \\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\dfrac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\dfrac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\n\nNow we can substitute this back into the original expression:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169}{36}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\dfrac{13}{6}\n\\]\n\nSo the simplified fraction is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\dfrac{13}{6}}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational\r\n\r\n# Define the terms\r\nterm1 = Rational(5, sqrt(80))\r\nterm2 = sqrt(845) / 9\r\nterm3 = sqrt(45)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the terms\r\nterm1_simplified = term1.simplify()\r\nterm2_simplified = term2.simplify()\r\nterm3_simplified = term3.simplify()\r\n\r\n# Combine the terms\r\nnumerator = term1_simplified + term2_simplified + term3_simplified\r\ndenominator = sqrt(5)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nexpression = numerator / denominator\r\nsimplified_expression = expression.simplify()\r\n\r\n# Take the square root of the simplified expression\r\nfinal_result = sqrt(simplified_expression)\r\nprint(final_result)\n```", "To simplify the given expression, we can break it down step-by-step.\n\nThe given expression is:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} + \\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} + \\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify the terms inside the fraction:\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\frac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\frac{\\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5}}{9} = \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n\\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nNow we can substitute these simplified terms back into the expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]\n\nTo combine the terms in the numerator, we need a common denominator:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} = \\frac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} = \\frac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad 3\\sqrt{5} = \\frac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\frac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\frac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{\\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{169}{36}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we take the square root of \\(\\frac{169}{36}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{169}{36}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\frac{13}{6}\n\\]\n\nSo the simplified fraction is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nnumerator = sp.Rational(5, sp.sqrt(80)) + sp.sqrt(845)/9 + sp.sqrt(45)\r\ndenominator = sp.sqrt(5)\r\nexpression = sp.sqrt(numerator / denominator)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = sp.simplify(expression)\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```", "To solve the given expression \\(\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}+\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}+\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt5}}\\), we will simplify it step by step.\n\n1. First, simplify the terms inside the fraction.\n2. Combine the simplified terms.\n3. Simplify the entire fraction.\n4. Finally, take the square root of the simplified fraction.\n\nLet's break it down and solve it using Python.\n\nFirst, we simplify \\(\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n\\[\n\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\dfrac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify \\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5}}{9} = \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}.\n\\]\n\nThen, we simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we combine these terms:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}.\n\\]\n\nTo combine these terms, we need a common denominator. The least common multiple of 4, 9, and 1 is 36. So we rewrite each term with the common denominator:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} = \\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} = \\dfrac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad 3\\sqrt{5} = \\dfrac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36}.\n\\]\n\nCombining these, we get:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\dfrac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\dfrac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we simplify the entire fraction:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169}{36}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\dfrac{13}{6}.\n\\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\dfrac{13}{6}}.\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational\r\n\r\n# Define the terms\r\nterm1 = Rational(5, sqrt(80))\r\nterm2 = sqrt(845) / 9\r\nterm3 = sqrt(45)\r\n\r\n# Combine the terms\r\nnumerator = term1 + term2 + term3\r\ndenominator = sqrt(5)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the fraction\r\nfraction = numerator / denominator\r\nsimplified_fraction = fraction.simplify()\r\n\r\n# Take the square root of the simplified fraction\r\nfinal_result = sqrt(simplified_fraction)\r\nprint(final_result)\n```", "To simplify the given expression, we will break it down step-by-step and use Python to ensure accuracy. The expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} + \\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} + \\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify the individual components of the expression:\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\frac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{5\\sqrt{5}}{20} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n\\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these simplified components back into the expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine the terms in the numerator:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5} = \\frac{9\\sqrt{5} + 52\\sqrt{5} + 108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{169}{36}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we take the square root of \\(\\frac{169}{36}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{169}{36}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\frac{13}{6}\n\\]\n\nSo the simplified fraction is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Calculate each part of the expression\r\nterm1 = 5 / math.sqrt(80)\r\nterm2 = math.sqrt(845) / 9\r\nterm3 = math.sqrt(45)\r\n\r\n# Sum the terms in the numerator\r\nnumerator = term1 + term2 + term3\r\n\r\n# Denominator is sqrt(5)\r\ndenominator = math.sqrt(5)\r\n\r\n# Full expression\r\nexpression_value = math.sqrt(numerator / denominator)\r\n\r\n# Simplified fraction\r\nsimplified_fraction = expression_value\r\n\r\nprint(simplified_fraction)\n```", "To simplify the given expression, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Simplify each term in the numerator separately.\n2. Sum the simplified terms in the numerator.\n3. Divide the resulting sum by \\(\\sqrt{5}\\).\n4. Take the square root of the resulting fraction.\n\nLet's break down each step in detail.\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\frac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n   \\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n   So,\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n   \\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n\n4. Sum the simplified terms in the numerator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5} = \\frac{9\\sqrt{5} + 52\\sqrt{5} + 108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n   \\]\n\n5. Divide the resulting sum by \\(\\sqrt{5}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{169}{36}\n   \\]\n\n6. Take the square root of the resulting fraction:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{169}{36}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\frac{13}{6}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the simplified expression is \\(\\frac{13}{6}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational\r\n\r\n# Define each term\r\nterm1 = Rational(5, 1) / sqrt(80)\r\nterm2 = sqrt(845) / 9\r\nterm3 = sqrt(45)\r\n\r\n# Sum the terms in the numerator\r\nnumerator = term1 + term2 + term3\r\n\r\n# Divide by sqrt(5)\r\nfraction = numerator / sqrt(5)\r\n\r\n# Take the square root of the resulting fraction\r\nresult = sqrt(fraction)\r\n\r\nprint(result.simplify())\n```\n```output\n13/6\n```\nThe simplified expression is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\\).", "To simplify the given expression, let's break it down step by step.\n\nThe expression is:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} + \\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} + \\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\n1. First, simplify the terms inside the square root in the numerator:\n   - Simplify $\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}$: \n     \\[\n     \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\frac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{5 \\cdot \\sqrt{5}}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n     \\]\n   - Simplify $\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}$:\n     \\[\n     \\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n     \\]\n     So,\n     \\[\n     \\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n     \\]\n   - Simplify $\\sqrt{45}$:\n     \\[\n     \\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n     \\]\n\n2. Now, combine these simplified terms:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}\n   \\]\n   To combine these, we need a common denominator. The common denominator for 4, 9, and 1 is 36:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} = \\frac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} = \\frac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36}, \\quad 3\\sqrt{5} = \\frac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n   \\]\n   So,\n   \\[\n   \\frac{9\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\frac{52\\sqrt{5}}{36} + \\frac{108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n   \\]\n\n3. Now, substitute this back into the original expression:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{169}{36}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\frac{13}{6}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the simplified fraction is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Define the terms\r\nterm1 = 5 / math.sqrt(80)\r\nterm2 = math.sqrt(845) / 9\r\nterm3 = math.sqrt(45)\r\n\r\n# Combine the terms in the numerator\r\nnumerator = term1 + term2 + term3\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nresult = math.sqrt(numerator / math.sqrt(5))\r\n\r\n# Display the result\r\nprint(result)\n```", "To solve the given expression, we will break it down step by step. The expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}+\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}+\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we will simplify the individual terms inside the fraction:\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n\\[\n\\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\dfrac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\dfrac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\dfrac{5\\sqrt{5}}{20} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n\\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nNow we substitute these simplified terms back into the expression:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine the terms in the numerator:\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\dfrac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5} = \\dfrac{9\\sqrt{5} + 52\\sqrt{5} + 108\\sqrt{5}}{36} = \\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36}}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169\\sqrt{5}}{36\\sqrt{5}}} = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{169}{36}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{169}}{\\sqrt{36}} = \\dfrac{13}{6}\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified fraction is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\dfrac{13}{6}}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\nfrom sympy import sqrt, Rational\r\n\r\n# Define the expression components\r\nnumerator = Rational(5, sqrt(80)) + sqrt(845)/9 + sqrt(45)\r\ndenominator = sqrt(5)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = sqrt(numerator / denominator)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the result to a fraction\r\nsimplified_fraction = simplified_expression.simplify()\r\nprint(simplified_fraction)\n```", 'Simplify the following expression to a simplified fraction: $$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{20}+\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}.$$ Shay\nSimplify the following expression to a simplified fraction: $$\\dfrac{6}{\\sqrt{21}+\\sqrt{7}+2\\sqrt{3}+2}.$$ Shay\nSimplify the following expression to a simplified fraction: $$\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{1-\\sqrt{3}}.$$ Shay\nSimplify the following expression to a simplified fraction: $$\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}}{1-\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}}.$$ Shay\nSimplify the following expression to a simplified fraction: $$\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{6}}{1-\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{6}}.$$ Shay\nSimplify the following expression to a simplified fraction: $$\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{6}}{1-\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{6}}.$$ Shay\nSimplify the following expression to a simplified fraction: $$\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{6}}{1+\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{6}}.$$ Shay\nSimplify the following expression to a simplified fraction: $$\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{6}}{1+\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{6}}.$$ Shay\nSimplify the following expression to a simplified fraction: $$\\dfrac{1-\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{6}}