 \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and between \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\).\n\nGiven:\n1. The angle between \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) is \\(29^\\circ\\).\n2. The angle between \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\) is \\(84^\\circ\\).\n\nWe can use the following steps to find the required angle:\n\n1. Use the given angles to set up vector equations.\n2. Use vector algebra to express \\(\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\) in terms of \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\).\n3. Calculate the dot product of \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\).\n4. Use the dot product to find the angle between \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\).\n\nLet's proceed with the Python code to perform these calculations.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the vectors a and b\na = sp.MatrixSymbol('a', 3, 1)\nb = sp.MatrixSymbol('b', 3, 1)\n\n# Define the angle between a and b\ntheta_ab = 29 * sp.pi / 180  # Convert to radians\n\n# Define the angle between b and a - b\ntheta_ba_b = 84 * sp.pi / 180  # Convert to radians\n\n# Define the dot product of a and b\ndot_ab = a.dot(b)\n\n# Define the dot product of b and a - b\ndot_ba_b = b.dot(a - b)\n\n# Use the given angles to set up equations\neq1 = sp.Eq(dot_ab, sp.cos(theta_ab))\neq2 = sp.Eq(dot_ba_b, sp.cos(theta_ba_b))\n\n# Solve for the dot product of a and a - b\ndot_aa_b = a.dot(a - b)\n\n# Use the dot product to find the angle between a and a - b\ncos_theta_a_aa_b = dot_aa_b / (a.norm() * (a - b).norm())\n\n# Calculate the angle in radians and then convert to degrees\ntheta_a_aa_b = sp.acos(cos_theta_a_aa_b)\ntheta_a_aa_b_deg = sp.deg(theta_a_aa_b)\n\n# Print the final angle in degrees\nprint(theta_a_aa_b_deg)\n```\n\nThe output will be the angle between \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\) in degrees. Let's run the code to get the result.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the vectors a and b\na = sp.MatrixSymbol('a', 3, 1)\nb = sp.Matri