w, let's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient using the formula\nn = 31\nk = 3\nbinomial_coefficient = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(binomial_coefficient)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of $\\dbinom{31}{28}$ is $\\boxed{4495}$.", "To compute \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\), we can use the formula for combinations, which is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, \\(n = 31\\) and \\(k = 28\\). So we need to compute:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!(31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this expression by canceling out the common factorial terms in the numerator and the denominator. This simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this step by step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculate the combination using the formula\nn = 31\nk = 28\n\n# Simplify the combination formula\ncombination = (n * (n-1) * (n-2)) // (3 * 2 * 1)\nprint(combination)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).", 'The binomial coefficient $\\binom{31}{28}$ can be computed using the formula $\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$. Here, $n = 31$ and $k = 28$, so we have:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot (31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29 \\times 28!}{28! \\times 3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{26970}{6} = 4495\n\\]\n\nWe can use Python to verify this calculation.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient using math.comb\nbinomial_coefficient = math.comb(31, 28)\nprint(binomial_coefficient)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe binomial coefficient $\\binom{31}{28}$ is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).', "To compute \\(\\binom{31}{28}\\), we can use the formula for binomial coefficients:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = 