ay piece is \\( \\frac{12}{5} \\) square inches.\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given data\ntotal_area_square = 16  # Area of the square ABCD\narea_square_e = total_area_square / 4  # Area of the square piece "e"\nremaining_area = total_area_square - area_square_e  # Remaining area for the five triangles\narea_gray_piece = remaining_area / 5  # Area of one of the isosceles triangles (gray piece)\n\nprint(area_gray_piece)\n```\n```output\n2.4\n```\nThe area of the gray piece is \\( \\frac{12}{5} = 2.4 \\) square inches.\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{2.4}\\).', "The area of the gray piece can be calculated by determining the area of the triangles it forms. The gray piece is a right triangle with legs of length 2 inches each. The area of a right triangle is given by the formula \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}\\). In this case, the base and height are both 2 inches, so the area is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 2 \\times 2 = 2 \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the base and height of the gray triangle\nbase = 2\nheight = 2\n\n# Calculate the area of the gray triangle\narea_gray_piece = 0.5 * base * height\nprint(area_gray_piece)\n```\n```output\n2.0\n```\nThe area of the gray piece is \\(\\boxed{2}\\) square inches.", 'To solve this problem, we need to understand the geometric properties and areas of the tangram pieces. The tangram consists of seven pieces: five isosceles triangles, one square (piece "e"), and one parallelogram (which is not shown in the diagram). The total area of the square is 16 square inches, so each side of the square is 4 inches.\n\nThe tangram pieces are derived from the square by cutting it into smaller shapes. The gray piece in the diagram is one of the isosceles triangles. Since the tangram is a dissection of the square into seven pieces, the total area of all the pieces combined 