he tetrahedron is an equilateral triangle, and the centroid (center) of the triangle with vertices \\((A, B, C)\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Centroid} = \\left(\\frac{A_x + B_x + C_x}{3}, \\frac{A_y + B_y +", "To solve this problem, we need to convert the decimal number \\(629_{10}\\) to its base 7 and base 8 representations. Then, we will compare the digits of these representations to find out how many digits are the same.\n\nLet's start by converting \\(629_{10}\\) to base 7 and base 8.\n\n### Conversion to Base 7\n\nTo convert a number to base 7, we repeatedly divide the number by 7 and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n629 \\div 7 &= 89 \\text{ remainder } 6 \\\\\n89 \\div 7 &= 12 \\text{ remainder } 5 \\\\\n12 \\div 7 &= 1 \\text{ remainder } 5 \\\\\n1 \\div 7 &= 0 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(629_{10} = 1556_7\\).\n\n### Conversion to Base 8\n\nTo convert a number to base 8, we repeatedly divide the number by 8 and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n629 \\div 8 &= 78 \\text{ remainder } 5 \\\\\n78 \\div 8 &= 9 \\text{ remainder } 6 \\\\\n9 \\div 8 &= 1 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\\\\n1 \\div 8 &= 0 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(629_{10} = 1165_8\\).\n\n### Comparing the Digits\n\nNow we compare the digits of \\(1556_7\\) and \\(1165_8\\):\n\n- \\(1556_7\\) has digits: 1, 5, 5, 6\n- \\(1165_8\\) has digits: 1, 1, 6, 5\n\nThe digits that appear in both representations are 1, 5, and 6. Therefore, there are 3 digits that are the same.\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to convert a decimal number to a given base\r\ndef convert_to_base(n, base):\r\n    digits = []\r\n    while n:\r\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\r\n        n //= base\r\n    return digits[::-1]\r\n\r\n# Convert 629 to base 7 and base 8\r\