saved = 800 gallons - 250 gallons = 550 gallons\n\nTherefore, Karla would have saved \\(\\boxed{550}\\) gallons of gasoline last year by driving a fuel-efficient hybrid car instead of an SUV.', 'To determine how many gallons of gasoline Karla would have saved by driving a fuel-efficient hybrid car instead of her SUV, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total gallons of gasoline used by the SUV:**\n   - The SUV averages 15 miles per gallon.\n   - Karla drove 12,000 miles.\n   - Using the formula for gallons used: \n     \\[\n     \\text{Gallons used by SUV} = \\frac{\\text{Total miles driven}}{\\text{Miles per gallon of SUV}}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gallons used by SUV} = \\frac{12,000 \\text{ miles}}{15 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = 800 \\text{ gallons}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total gallons of gasoline used by the hybrid car:**\n   - The hybrid car averages 48 miles per gallon.\n   - Karla drove 12,000 miles.\n   - Using the formula for gallons used:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gallons used by hybrid car} = \\frac{\\text{Total miles driven}}{\\text{Miles per gallon of hybrid car}}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gallons used by hybrid car} = \\frac{12,000 \\text{ miles}}{48 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = 250 \\text{ gallons}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the gallons of gasoline saved by driving the hybrid car:**\n   - Subtract the gallons used by the hybrid car from the gallons used by the SUV:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gallons saved} = \\text{Gallons used by SUV} - \\text{Gallons used by hybrid car}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Gallons saved} = 800 \\text{ gallons} - 250 \\text{ gallons} = 550 \\text{ gallons}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, Karla would have saved \\(\\boxed{550}\\) gallons of gasoline last year had she driven a fuel-efficient hybrid car instead of her SUV.', 'To determine how many gallons of gasoline Karla would have saved by driving a fuel-efficient hybrid car instead of her SUV, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the total gallons of gasoline used by the SUV:**\n   - Karla drove 12,000 miles.\n   - The SUV averages 15 miles per gallon.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Gallons used by SUV} = \\frac{\\text{Total miles driven}}{\\text{Miles per gallon of SUV}} = \\frac{12,000 \\text{ miles}}{15 \\text{ miles/gallon}} = 800 \\text{ gallons}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total gallons of gasoline used by the hybrid car:**\n   - Karla drove 12,000 miles.\n   - The hybrid car averages 48 miles per gallon.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Gallons used by hybrid car} = \\frac{\\text{Total miles driven}}{\\text{Miles per gallon of hybrid car}} = \\frac{12,000 \\text{ miles}}{48 \\text{ miles/gallon}} = 250 \\text{ gallons}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the gallons of gasoline saved by driving the hybrid car:**\n   - Subtract the gallons used by the hybrid car from the gallons used by the SUV.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Gallons saved} = \\text{Gallons used by SUV} - \\text{Gallons used by hybrid car} = 800 \\text{ gallons} - 250 \\text{ gallons} = 550 \\text{ gallons}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Karla would have saved \\boxed{550} gallons of gasoline last year had she driven a fuel-efficient hybrid car instead of an SUV.', 'To determine how many gallons of gasoline Karla would have saved by driving a fuel-efficient hybrid car instead of her SUV, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the amount of gasoline used by the SUV.\n2. Calculate the amount of gasoline used by the hybrid car.\n3. Find the difference between the gasoline used by the SUV and the hybrid car.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the amount of gasoline used by the SUV.**\n\nThe SUV averages 15 miles per gallon. Therefore, the amount of gasoline used by the SUV to drive 12,000 miles is:\n\\[\n\\text{Gasoline used by SUV} = \\frac{12,000 \\text{ miles}}{15 \\text{ miles per gallon}} = 800 \\text{ gallons}\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the amount of gasoline used by the hybrid car.**\n\nThe hybrid car averages 48 miles per gallon. Therefore, the amount of gasoline used by 