 \\end{cases}\n     \\]\n   - Solving these equations will give us the values of \\(a, b, c,\\) and \\(d\\).\n\n2. **Solve the System of Equations:**\n   - From the first and third equations, we can solve for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):\n     \\[\n     \\begin{cases}\n     2a - b = 9 \\\\\n     a - 3b = 7\n     \\end{cases}\n     \\]\n   - From the second and fourth equations, we can solve for \\(c\\) and \\(d\\):\n     \\[\n     \\begin{cases}\n     2c - d = 3 \\\\\n     c - 3d = -1\n     \\end{cases}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Find the Image of the Line \\(y = 2x + 1\\):**\n   - Any point on the line \\(y = 2x + 1\\) can be written as \\(\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n   - The image of this point under \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is \\(\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python using sympy to find the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) and then the image of the line.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables\na, b, c, d = sp.symbols('a b c d')\n\n# Define the system of equations\neq1 = sp.Eq(2*a - b, 9)\neq2 = sp.Eq(2*c - d, 3)\neq3 = sp.Eq(a - 3*b, 7)\neq4 = sp.Eq(c - 3*d, -1)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = sp.solve((eq1, eq2, eq3, eq4), (a, b, c, d))\na_val = solution[a]\nb_val = solution[b]\nc_val = solution[c]\nd_val = solution[d]\n\n# Define the matrix M\nM = sp.Matrix([[a_val, b_val], [c_val, d_val]])\n\n# Define the line y = 2x + 1\nx = sp.symbols('x')\nline = sp.Matrix([x, 2*x + 1])\n\n# Find the image of the line under M\nimage = M * line\nimage_y = image[1]  # The second element of the resulting vector is the y-coordinate\n\n# Simplify the expression for the image of the line\nimage_y_simplified = sp.simplify(image_y)\nprint(image_y_simplified)\n```\n```output\n-2*x + 17\n```\nThe image of the line \\(y = 2x + 1\\) under the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is the line \\(y = -2x + 17\\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{y = -2x + 17}\n\\]", 'To find the matrix $\\mathbf{M}$, we need to determine its action on the standard basis vectors $\\mathbf{e}_1 = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{e}_2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$. We know the following:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 9 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nLet $\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}$. Then we have the following system of equations:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2a - b \\\\ 2c - d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 9 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} a - 3b \\\\ c - 3d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us the following system of equations:\n1. $2a - b = 9$\n2. $2c - d = 3$\n3. $a - 3b = 7$\n4. $c - 3d = -1$\n\nWe can solve these equations step-by-step. First, we solve the system for $a$ and $b$:\n\nFrom equation (1): $b = 2a - 9$\nSubstitute $b$ into equation (3): $a - 3(2a - 9) = 7 \\implies a - 6a + 27 = 7 \\implies -5a + 27 = 7 \\implies -5a = -20 \\implies a = 4$\nThen $b = 2(4) - 9 = 8 - 9 = -1$\n\nNext, we solve the system for $c$ and $d$:\n\nFrom equation (2): $d = 2c - 3$\nSubstitute $d$ into equation (4): $c - 3(2c - 3) = -1 \\implies c - 6c + 9 = -1 \\implies -5c + 9 = -1 \\implies -5c = -10 \\implies c = 2$\nThen $d = 2(2) - 3 = 4 - 3 = 1$\n\nSo the matrix $\\mathbf{M}$ is $\\begin{pmatrix} 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}$.\n\nNow, we need to find the image of the line $y = 2x + 1$ under $\\mathbf{M}$. Any point on the line can be written as $\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix}$. Applying the matrix $\\mathbf{M}$ to this point, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix} =