onships in the diagram:\n\n1. Since \\(\\overline{ST} \\parallel \\overline{QR}\\), the corresponding angles and alternate interior angles will be equal.\n2. The angle \\(\\angle STR\\) is an exterior angle to the triangle \\(\\triangle PST\\). The measure of an exterior angle of a triangle is equal to the sum of the measures of the two non-adjacent interior angles.\n\nHere, \\(\\angle STR\\) is the exterior angle to \\(\\triangle PST\\), and the two non-adjacent interior angles are \\(\\angle P\\) and \\(\\angle Q\\).\n\nSo, \\(\\angle STR = \\angle P + \\angle Q = 40^\\circ + 35^\\circ = 75^\\circ\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the calculation is accurate.\n```python\n# Given angles\nangle_P = 40\nangle_Q = 35\n\n# Calculate the measure of angle STR\nangle_STR = angle_P + angle_Q\nprint(angle_STR)\n```\n```output\n75\n```\nThe measure of \\(\\angle STR\\) is \\(\\boxed{75}\\) degrees.", "To solve the problem, we need to use the properties of parallel lines and angles. Here's the step-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. Since \\(\\overline{ST} \\parallel \\overline{QR}\\), the corresponding angles and alternate interior angles formed by the transversal line will be equal.\n2. We know that \\(\\angle Q = 35^\\circ\\). Since \\(\\overline{ST} \\parallel \\overline{QR}\\), the corresponding angle to \\(\\angle Q\\) on line \\(\\overline{ST}\\) will also be \\(35^\\circ\\). This means \\(\\angle STR = 35^\\circ\\).\n3. We don't need to consider \\(\\angle P = 40^\\circ\\) for this specific problem because we are only asked to find \\(\\angle STR\\), and it is directly related to \\(\\angle Q\\) due to the parallel lines.\n\nSo, the measure of \\(\\angle STR\\) is \\(35^\\circ\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with a simple Python code using sympy to ensure the result is accurate.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the angles\nangle_Q = 35\n\n# Since ST is parallel to QR, angle STR is equal to angle Q\nangle_STR = angle_Q\n\nprint(angle_STR)\n```\n```output