ings in dollars} = 27.47 + 35.23 + 37.37 + 26.52\n\\]\n\nNext, we convert the total earnings into cents:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total earnings in cents} = \\text{Total earnings in dollars} \\times 100\n\\]\n\nFinally, we find the remainder when the total amount in cents is divided by 100:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Remainder} = \\text{Total earnings in cents} \\mod 100\n\\]\n\nLet's implement this in Python to get the accurate result.\n```python\n# Earnings in dollars\nearnings = [27.47, 35.23, 37.37, 26.52]\n\n# Sum up the earnings\ntotal_earnings_dollars = sum(earnings)\n\n# Convert the total earnings into cents\ntotal_earnings_cents = int(total_earnings_dollars * 100)\n\n# Find the remainder when the total amount in cents is divided by 100\nremainder_cents = total_earnings_cents % 100\n\nprint(remainder_cents)\n```\n```output\n99\n```\nThe remainder when the total amount of money, in cents, is divided by 100 is \\(\\boxed{99}\\).", 'A rectangular prism has a length of 3 inches, a width of 4 inches, and a height of 5 inches. What is the surface area, in square inches, of this prism? \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\box