52\n\n# Total amount earned\ntotal_earned = linda_earned + sherry_earned + june_earned + connie_earned\n\n# Convert total amount to cents\ntotal_cents = int(total_earned * 100)\n\n# Calculate the number of whole dollars that can be made\nwhole_dollars = total_cents // 100\n\n# Calculate the leftover cents\nleftover_cents = total_cents % 100\n\nprint(leftover_cents)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nAfter converting as many of the coins into bills as they could, the amount of money left is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cents.", 'Linda, Sherry, June, and Connie walked around their neighborhoods selling girl scout cookies. Linda earned $\\$27.47$, Sherry earned $\\$35.23$, June earned $\\$37.37$, and Connie earned $\\$26.52$. After the sale, they pooled their money together and went to the bank to convert the coins into dollars. How much money, in cents, was left after they converted as many of the coins into bills as they could?', 'Given that $60\\%$ of the students at a school are girls, $40\\%$ of the students bring their lunch to school, and $80\\%$ of the students who bring their lunch are girls, what is the probability that a girl brings her lunch to school?  \\[\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{1}{10} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1}{9} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{1}{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\frac{1}{5}\\] \\[\\textbf{(F) }\\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(G) }\\frac{1}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(H) }\\frac{2}{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(I) }\\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(J) }\\frac{3}{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(K) }\\frac{2}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(L) }\\frac{5}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(M) }\\frac{3}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(N) }\\frac{4}{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(O) }\\frac{5}{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(P) }\\frac{6}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(Q) }\\frac{7}{8} \\qquad \\textbf{(R) }\\frac{8}{9} \\qquad \\textbf{(S) }\\frac{9}{10} \\qquad \\textbf{(T) }\\frac{5}{9}\\] \\[\\textbf{(U) }1 \\qquad \\textbf{(V) }\\text{The answer is not listed above.}\\] \\[\\textbf{(W) } \\text{No Solution} \\qquad \\textbf{(X