int(area)\n```\n```output\n15.0\n```\nThe area of the shaded triangle is \\(\\boxed{15}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the shaded triangle, we need to use the given dimensions of the rectangle and the coordinates of the vertices of the triangle. The vertices of the triangle are at (0,0), (2,3), and (10,0).\n\nThe formula for the area of a triangle given its vertices \\((x_1, y_1)\\), \\((x_2, y_2)\\), and \\((x_3, y_3)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \\right|\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the coordinates of the vertices (0,0), (2,3), and (10,0) into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0(3 - 0) + 2(0 - 0) + 10(0 - 3) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 + 0 + 10(-3) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| -30 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 30 = 15\n\\]\n\nSo, the area of the shaded triangle is \\(15 \\text{ cm}^2\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to calculate the area of a triangle given its vertices\ndef triangle_area(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3):\n    return 0.5 * abs(x1*(y2 - y3) + x2*(y3 - y1) + x3*(y1 - y2))\n\n# Coordinates of the vertices of the triangle\nx1, y1 = 0, 0\nx2, y2 = 2, 3\nx3, y3 = 10, 0\n\n# Calculate the area of the triangle\narea = triangle_area(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3)\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n15.0\n```\nThe area of the shaded triangle is \\(\\boxed{15}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the area of the shaded triangle, we need to use the formula for the area of a triangle, which is given by:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} \\]\n\nFrom the diagram, we can see that the base of the triangle is 10 cm and the height is 3 cm. Therefore, we can substitute these values into the formula to get the area.\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Base and height of the triangle\nbase = 10\nheight = 3\n\n# Area of the triangle\narea = 0.5 * base * height\npri