 right side, \\(x = 10\\) is indeed a solution. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the accuracy of the result.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Define the equation\nequation = sp.sqrt(x + sp.sqrt(3*x + 6)) + sp.sqrt(x - sp.sqrt(3*x + 6)) - 6\n\n# Solve the equation\nsolution = sp.solve(equation, x)\nprint(solution)\n```", "To solve the equation \\(\\sqrt{x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}} + \\sqrt{x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}} = 6\\), let's denote \\(y = \\sqrt{x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}}\\) and \\(z = \\sqrt{x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}}\\). Then the equation becomes \\(y + z = 6\\).\n\nNow, let's square both \\(y\\) and \\(z\\) to get rid of the square roots:\n\\[y^2 = x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}\\]\n\\[z^2 = x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}\\]\n\nAdding these two equations, we get:\n\\[y^2 + z^2 = (x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}) + (x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}) = 2x\\]\n\nSince \\(y + z = 6\\), we can square this equation as well:\n\\[(y + z)^2 = y^2 + z^2 + 2yz = 36\\]\n\\[2x + 2yz = 36\\]\n\\[x + yz = 18\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\(yz\\). We know that:\n\\[y^2 - z^2 = (x + \\sqrt{3x + 6}) - (x - \\sqrt{3x + 6}) = 2\\sqrt{3x + 6}\\]\n\\[(y + z)(y - z) = 2\\sqrt{3x + 6}\\]\n\\[6(y - z) = 2\\sqrt{3x + 6}\\]\n\\[y - z = \\frac{\\sqrt{3x + 6}}{3}\\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations in terms of \\(y\\) and \\(z\\):\n\\[y + z = 6\\]\n\\[y - z = \\frac{\\sqrt{3x + 6}}{3}\\]\n\nAdding these two equations, we get:\n\\[2y = 6 + \\frac{\\sqrt{3x + 6}}{3}\\]\n\\[y = 3 + \\frac{\\sqrt{3x + 6}}{6}\\]\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first, we get:\n\\[2z = 6 - \\frac{\\sqrt{3x + 6}}{3}\\]\n\\[z = 3 - \\frac{\\sqrt{3x + 6}}{6}\\]\n\nNow we can find \\(yz\\):\n\\[yz = \\left(3 + \\frac{\\sqrt{3x + 6}}{6}\\right)\\left(3 - \\frac{\\sqrt{3x + 6}}{6}\\right) = 9 - \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3x + 6}}{6}\\right)^2 = 9 - \\frac{3x + 6}{36} = 9 - \\frac{x + 2}{12} = 9 - \\frac{x}{12} - \\frac{1}{6}\\]\n\\[yz = \\frac{108 - x - 2}{12} 