er_square_rounded} square units")\n```\n```output\nOriginal price of the shirt: 36.0 dollars\nArea of the inner square: 50 square units\n```\nThe original price of the shirt is $\\boxed{36}$ dollars, and the area of the inner square is $\\boxed{50}$ square units.', 'A rectangle has area $16$ and perimeter $20$. What is the length of its diagonal? \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \