 \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}.', "To solve the problem, we need to find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), where \\( 0 < p < 15 \\).\n\nLet's break down the function \\( f(x) \\):\n\n1. When \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\)\n   - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\)\n   - \\( |x - p - 15| = 15 + p - x \\)\n\nSo, the function becomes:\n\\[ f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (15 + p - x) = 30 - x \\]\n\nSince \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) is a decreasing function in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in this interval will occur at \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nNow, let's evaluate \\( f(x) \\) at \\( x = 15 \\):\n\\[ f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15 \\]\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Set the interval p <= x <= 15 and the range of p (0 < p < 15)\np_values = [1, 5, 10, 14]  # Example values for p within the range (0, 15)\nresults = []\n\n# Calculate the minimum value of f(x) for each p in the interval p <= x <= 15\nfor p in p_values:\n    min_value = min(f(x, p) for x in range(p, 16))\n    results.append(min_value)\n\nprint(results)\n```\n```output\n[15, 15, 15, 15]\n```\nThe results confirm that for different values of \\( p \\) within the range \\( 0 < p < 15 \\), the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is consistently 15.\n\nTherefore, the minimum value taken by \\( f(x) \\) for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", ' 1. First, we need to understand the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\). Since \\( p \\) is between 0 and 15, the critical points for the absolute value functions are \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 