 \\( x = p \\), \\( f(p) = 30 - p \\)\n- At \\( x = 15 \\), \\( f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15 \\)\n\nSince \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) is a decreasing function, the minimum value occurs at the right endpoint of the interval, which is \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the interval p <= x <= 15\np = 5  # Example value for p, any value in the range 0 < p < 15 will work\nx_values = [p, 15]  # Endpoints of the interval\n\n# Calculate the function values at the endpoints\nf_p = f(p, p)\nf_15 = f(15, p)\n\n# Determine the minimum value\nmin_value = min(f_p, f_15)\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\n15\n```\nThe minimum value taken by the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", 'Let $f(x)=|x-p|+|x-15|+|x-p-15|,$ where $0 < p < 15.$ Determine the minimum value taken by $f(x)$ for $x$ in the interval $p \\leq x\\leq15.$\nLet $f(x)=|x-p|+|x-15|+|x-p-15|,$ where $0 < p < 15.$ Determine the minimum value taken by $f(x)$ for $x$ in the interval $p \\leq x\\leq15.$\nLet $f(x)=|x-p|+|x-15|+|x-p-15|,$ where $0 < p < 15.$ Determine the minimum value taken by $f(x)$ for $x$ in the interval $p \\leq x\\leq15.$\nLet $f(x)=|x-p|+|x-15|+|x-p-15|,$ where $0 < p < 15.$ Determine the minimum value taken by $f(x)$ for $x$ in the interval $p \\leq x\\leq15.$\nLet $f(x)=|x-p|+|x-15|+|x-p-15|,$ where $0 < p < 15.$ Determine the minimum value taken by $f(x)$ for $x$ in the interval $p \\leq x\\leq15.$\nLet $f(x)=|x-p|+|x-15|+|x-p-15|,$ where $0 < p < 15.$ Determine the minimum value taken by $f(x)$ for $x$ in the interval $p \\leq x\\leq15.$\nLet $f(x)=|x-p|+|x-15|+|x-p-15|,$ where $0 < p < 15.$ Determine the minimum value taken by $f(x)$ for $x$ in the interval $p \\leq x\\leq15.$\nLet $f(x)=|x-p