ts:\n    a_n_minus_1 = calculate_a_n_minus_1(roots)\n    if abs(a_n_minus_1) < min_abs_a_n_minus_1:\n        min_abs_a_n_minus_1 = abs(a_n_minus_1)\n\nprint(min_abs_a_n_minus_1)\n```\n```output\n2\n```\nThe least possible value of \\(|a_{n-1}|\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to consider the polynomial \\(f(x) = 2x^n + a_{n-1}x^{n-1} + \\cdots + a_2x^2 + a_1x + 66\\) with integer coefficients and distinct integer roots. Let's denote the roots of the polynomial by \\(r_1, r_2, \\ldots, r_n\\). By Vieta's formulas, we know that:\n\n1. The sum of the roots (taken one at a time) is \\(-\\frac{a_{n-1}}{a_n} = -\\frac{a_{n-1}}{2}\\).\n2. The product of the roots is \\((-1)^n \\frac{a_0}{a_n} = (-1)^n \\frac{66}{2} = (-1)^n \\cdot 33\\).\n\nSince the roots are distinct integers, let's consider the possible factorizations of 33 (considering the sign, since the product of the roots is 33 or -33). The factorizations of 33 are \\(\\pm 1 \\cdot \\pm 33\\), \\(\\pm 3 \\cdot \\pm 11\\), and \\(\\pm 1 \\cdot \\pm 3 \\cdot \\pm 11\\). To minimize \\(|a_{n-1}|\\), we need to find the combination of roots that gives the smallest possible value for the sum of the roots.\n\nLet's consider the possible sets of roots and calculate the corresponding \\(a_{n-1}\\):\n\n1. If the roots are \\(1, -1, 33, -33\\), the sum of the roots is \\(1 - 1 + 33 - 33 = 0\\), so \\(a_{n-1} = 0\\).\n2. If the roots are \\(1, -1, 3, -3\\), the sum of the roots is \\(1 - 1 + 3 - 3 = 0\\), so \\(a_{n-1} = 0\\).\n3. If the roots are \\(1, -1, 11, -11\\), the sum of the roots is \\(1 - 1 + 11 - 11 = 0\\), so \\(a_{n-1} = 0\\).\n4. If the roots are \\(1, 3, 11, -33\\), the sum of the roots is \\(1 + 3 + 11 - 33 = -18\\), so \\(a_{n-1} = 36\\).\n5. If the roots are \\(1, 3, -11, 33\\), the sum of the roots is \\(1 + 3 - 11 + 33 = 26\\), so \\(a_{n-1} = -52\\).\n6. If the roots are \\(1, -3, 11, 33\\), the sum of the roots is \\(1 - 3 + 11 + 33 = 42\\), so \\(a_{n-1} = -84\\).\n7. If the ro