hematically, this is represented as:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total number of personalities} = 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of choices for each part of the personality\nhairstyles = 3\neyebrows = 2\neyes = 1\nears = 2\nlips = 2\nshoes = 2\n\n# Total number of different personalities\ntotal_personalities = hairstyles * eyebrows * eyes * ears * lips * shoes\nprint(total_personalities)\n```\n```output\n48\n```\nThe total number of different wacky personalities Tom can come up with is \\(\\boxed{48}\\).", "To determine the total number of different wacky personalities Tom can create for his Mr. Potato Head, we need to consider all the possible combinations of the different components. Each component can be chosen independently, and we can optionally choose to include a hairstyle or not. This means for each component, we have a certain number of choices, and we need to multiply these choices together to get the total number of combinations.\n\nHere's the breakdown of the components and their respective choices:\n- 3 hairstyles (including the option of no hairstyle)\n- 2 sets of eyebrows\n- 1 pair of googly eyes (only one option)\n- 2 sets of ears\n- 2 sets of lips\n- 2 pairs of shoes (one regular and one clown)\n\nThe total number of different personalities can be calculated as follows:\n\\[ \\text{Total Personalities} = 4 \\times 2 \\times 1 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\]\nThe 4 comes from the 3 hairstyles plus the option of no hairstyle. The rest are the number of choices for each component.\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of choices for each component\nhair_styles = 3 + 1  # 3 hairstyles + 1 option for no hairstyle\neyebrows = 2\neyes = 1  # Only one pair of googly eyes\nears = 2\nlips = 2\nshoes = 2  # One regular and one clown\n\n# Total number of different personalities\ntotal_personalities = hair_styles * eyebrows * eyes * 